/* ============================================================
   NEGOTIABLE CLAUSE FAMILIES
   option: [label, lean, paragraphs, why for buy side, why for sell side, optional definitions]
   lean: -2 strongly favours the buy side ... +2 strongly favours the sell side
   tokens: {B} buy-side party, {S} sell-side party, {D} subject matter, {T} target,
           {N} this clause number, {R:key} cross-reference to another clause
   paragraph: "text" or ["lead-in", ["item", "item"], "optional tail"]
   ============================================================ */
const IPR_DEF = "patents, rights to inventions, copyright and related rights, trade marks, business names and domain names, rights in get-up, goodwill and the right to sue for passing off, rights in designs, rights in computer software, database rights, rights to use and protect the confidentiality of confidential information (including know-how and trade secrets) and all other intellectual property rights, in each case whether registered or unregistered and including all applications for, and renewals or extensions of, such rights, and all similar or equivalent rights or forms of protection in any part of the world";
const GIP_DEF = "the exercise of that degree of skill, care, prudence, efficiency, foresight and timeliness as would reasonably be expected from a skilled and experienced supplier engaged in the same type of undertaking under the same or similar circumstances";

const C = {
lol:{t:"Limitation of Liability",g:["liability","indemnities"],
 d:"Sets the most each party can be made to pay if things go wrong, and which kinds of loss cannot be claimed at all.",
 n:"Liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, and for fraud, can never be limited (Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977, s.2(1); HIH Casualty v Chase Manhattan [2003] UKHL 6). In standard terms, any other cap must satisfy the reasonableness test in the 1977 Act.",
 pre:[["Nothing in this Agreement shall limit or exclude either party's liability for:",["death or personal injury caused by its negligence, or the negligence of its employees, agents or subcontractors;","fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation; or","any other liability which cannot be limited or excluded by applicable law."]]],
 o:[
 ["{S} uncapped",-2,["Subject to clause {N}.1, {S}'s liability to {B} under or in connection with this Agreement, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty or otherwise, shall not be limited.","Subject to clause {N}.1, {B}'s total aggregate liability to {S} under or in connection with this Agreement shall not exceed the Charges paid by {B} in the twelve (12) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim."],
  "You can recover everything you lose, while your own exposure stays small.","There is no ceiling. One serious claim could cost more than the whole contract is worth."],
 ["Enhanced cap with carve-outs",-1,["Subject to clauses {N}.1 and {N}.3, each party's total aggregate liability under or in connection with this Agreement, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty or otherwise, shall not exceed, in respect of all claims arising in any Contract Year, an amount equal to two hundred per cent (200%) of the Charges paid or payable in that Contract Year.",["The limit in clause {N}.2 shall not apply to:",["breach of the confidentiality obligations in this Agreement;","breach of the data protection obligations in this Agreement;","liability under any indemnity given in this Agreement; or","{B}'s obligation to pay the Charges properly due."]]],
  "A generous cap, and the losses most likely to be catastrophic sit outside it.","Your exposure is twice a year's fees, and data and confidentiality claims are unlimited.",{"Contract Year":"each period of twelve (12) months beginning on the Effective Date or on any anniversary of it"}],
 ["Annual charges cap",1,["Subject to clause {N}.1, neither party shall be liable to the other, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty or otherwise, for any indirect or consequential loss.","Subject to clause {N}.1, each party's total aggregate liability under or in connection with this Agreement, whether arising in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty or otherwise, shall not exceed, in respect of all claims arising in any Contract Year, one hundred per cent (100%) of the Charges paid or payable in that Contract Year."],
  "Common and defensible, but if the contract fails badly your losses may exceed a year's fees. Note that excluding indirect or consequential loss removes only unusual losses under English law, so the cap does most of the work.","A sensible position. Your worst case roughly matches what you earn in a year.",{"Contract Year":"each period of twelve (12) months beginning on the Effective Date or on any anniversary of it"}],
 ["Low cap, key losses excluded",2,[["Subject to clause {N}.1, {S} shall not be liable to {B}, whether in contract, tort (including negligence), breach of statutory duty or otherwise, for any:",["loss of profits;","loss of revenue or anticipated savings;","loss or corruption of data;","loss of goodwill or reputation; or","indirect or consequential loss,"],"in each case whether direct or indirect."],"Subject to clause {N}.1, {S}'s total aggregate liability under or in connection with this Agreement shall not exceed the Charges paid by {B} in the three (3) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim."],
  "You would recover very little, and the losses most likely to hurt a business (profit and data) are excluded even where they are direct.","Your exposure is small and the expensive kinds of loss are off the table, though a court may test the clause for reasonableness."]]},

ind:{t:"Intellectual Property Indemnity",g:["indemnities","ip"],
 d:"Says who pays if a third party claims that what is supplied infringes its intellectual property.",
 n:"An indemnity is a promise to pay a defined loss. Unlike a damages claim, it does not depend on proving breach, and well-drafted wording can sidestep arguments about remoteness and mitigation.",
 df:{"Intellectual Property Rights":IPR_DEF,"IPR Claim":"any claim made against {B} alleging that the receipt, possession or use of {D} in accordance with this Agreement infringes the Intellectual Property Rights of a third party"},
 o:[
 ["Full and uncapped",-2,["{S} shall indemnify {B} and keep {B} indemnified in full against all losses, liabilities, damages, costs (including legal fees on a full indemnity basis) and expenses suffered or incurred by {B} arising out of or in connection with any IPR Claim.","The limitations of liability in this Agreement shall not apply to {S}'s liability under clause {N}.1."],
  "If anyone sues you over what you bought, the other side pays the whole bill, including your legal costs.","Unlimited exposure for risks you may not fully control, such as patents you did not know existed."],
 ["Indemnity with conduct and remedies",0,[["{S} shall indemnify {B} against all losses, liabilities, damages, costs (including reasonable legal fees) and expenses arising out of or in connection with any IPR Claim, provided that {B}:",["notifies {S} in writing of the IPR Claim promptly, and in any event within ten (10) Business Days of becoming aware of it;","makes no admission and enters into no settlement in relation to the IPR Claim without {S}'s prior written consent;","allows {S} sole conduct of the defence and settlement of the IPR Claim at {S}'s cost; and","gives {S} such reasonable assistance as it requests, at {S}'s cost."]],["If any IPR Claim is made, or in {S}'s reasonable opinion is likely to be made, {S} may at its option and expense:",["procure for {B} the right to continue using the affected items;","modify or replace the affected items so that they become non-infringing without any material reduction in performance or functionality; or","if neither of the above is reasonably practicable, terminate this Agreement in respect of the affected items and refund to {B} any Charges paid in advance for them."]]],
  "Solid protection, but you must follow the notice and conduct steps exactly or risk losing the cover.","The market position. You run the litigation and have ways to limit the damage if a claim lands."],
 ["Capped, with exclusions",1,["{S} shall indemnify {B} against all losses, liabilities, damages, costs and expenses arising out of or in connection with any IPR Claim, subject to {B} complying with the notice and conduct requirements reasonably specified by {S}.",["Clause {N}.1 shall not apply to the extent that an IPR Claim arises from:",["any modification of the affected items not made by or on behalf of {S};","{S}'s compliance with any specification, design or instruction provided by {B}; or","use of the affected items in combination with any item not supplied, or approved in writing, by {S}."]],"{S}'s liability under this clause is subject to the limitations of liability in this Agreement."],
  "Real gaps. Many infringement claims arise from how items are configured or combined, and those are excluded.","You only answer for problems you actually caused, and within your cap."],
 ["Fix or refund only",2,[["If an IPR Claim is made, {S}'s sole obligation, and {B}'s sole and exclusive remedy, shall be for {S}, at its option and expense, to:",["procure for {B} the right to continue using the affected items;","modify or replace the affected items so that they become non-infringing; or","terminate this Agreement in respect of the affected items and refund any Charges paid in advance for them."]]],
  "If you are sued, you bear the legal costs and any damages yourself.","Your only exposure is the cost of a fix or a refund."]]},

term:{t:"Termination for Convenience",g:["termination","penalties"],
 d:"Says whether a party can end the contract early without the other side having done anything wrong.",
 n:"A fee payable on exercising a right to terminate, rather than on breach, is generally outside the rule against penalties (Cavendish Square Holding v Makdessi [2015] UKSC 67).",
 o:[
 ["{B} may exit on 30 days",-2,["{B} may terminate this Agreement, in whole or in part, at any time by giving not less than thirty (30) days' written notice to {S}.","{B} shall have no liability to {S} in respect of any termination under clause {N}.1, other than to pay any sums which have accrued due to {S} at the date of termination."],
  "Maximum flexibility. You can leave as soon as your needs change.","Revenue becomes unpredictable, and you may lose the customer before recovering your set-up costs."],
 ["Mutual, after a minimum period",0,["Either party may terminate this Agreement by giving not less than ninety (90) days' written notice to the other, provided that no such notice may expire before the first anniversary of the Effective Date."],
  "You are committed for a year, then free to leave on fair notice.","A guaranteed first year and reasonable warning of any exit."],
 ["Exit on payment of a fee",1,["{B} may terminate this Agreement by giving not less than ninety (90) days' written notice to {S}, subject to paying {S} the Termination Fee within thirty (30) days of the date of termination.","The parties agree that the Termination Fee is proportionate to {S}'s legitimate interest in the continued performance of this Agreement."],
  "You can leave, but it will cost you a meaningful sum.","You recover much of the revenue you were counting on.",{"Termination Fee":"an amount equal to fifty per cent (50%) of the Charges that would have been payable from the date of termination until the expiry of the Initial Term"}],
 ["No early exit",2,["Neither party may terminate this Agreement for convenience before the expiry of the Initial Term."],
  "You are locked in for the full term, even if the contract stops suiting your business.","Your revenue is secure for the whole term."]]},

tmb:{t:"Termination for Cause",g:["termination"],
 d:"Says when a party can end the contract because the other has broken it or become insolvent.",
 n:"Without an express right, a party can terminate only for repudiatory breach, which is a high bar. Since the Corporate Insolvency and Governance Act 2020, a supplier generally cannot terminate a supply contract because the customer enters an insolvency procedure (Insolvency Act 1986, s.233B).",
 pre:["Either party may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect by giving written notice to the other party if the other party suspends, or threatens to suspend, payment of its debts, is unable to pay its debts within the meaning of section 123 of the Insolvency Act 1986, has an administrator, receiver or liquidator appointed, enters into any composition or arrangement with its creditors, or is subject to any analogous event in any jurisdiction, in each case to the extent permitted by law."],
 o:[
 ["Low threshold for {B}",-2,[["{B} may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect by giving written notice to {S} if {S}:",["commits any breach of this Agreement and fails to remedy it within ten (10) Business Days of being notified in writing to do so; or","commits a material breach of this Agreement, or a series of breaches which together amount to a material breach, whether or not capable of remedy."]]],
  "An easy exit if the other side underperforms.","You could lose the contract over minor or one-off problems."],
 ["Material breach, 30-day cure",0,["Either party may terminate this Agreement with immediate effect by giving written notice to the other party if the other party commits a material breach of this Agreement which is irremediable or, if remediable, which it fails to remedy within thirty (30) days of being notified in writing to do so."],
  "The market position. A clear exit, with a fair window for the other side to put things right.","A fair standard, and time to fix problems before you lose the contract."],
 ["Material breach after escalation",1,["Either party may terminate this Agreement by giving written notice to the other party if the other party commits a material breach of this Agreement which it fails to remedy within sixty (60) days of being notified in writing to do so, provided that the matter has first been referred for resolution under the dispute resolution procedure in this Agreement."],
  "You may have to live with poor performance for two months or more before you can leave.","Real time and a process to fix problems before the contract is at risk."],
 ["Narrow rights only",2,["{B} may terminate this Agreement by giving written notice to {S} only if {S} commits a material breach of this Agreement which is incapable of remedy.","{S} may terminate this Agreement by giving written notice to {B} if {B} fails to pay any undisputed amount within sixty (60) days of its due date."],
  "You are close to stuck, even when performance is poor.","Very hard for the other side to end the contract, while you keep an exit for non-payment."]]},

pay:{t:"Charges and Payment",g:["penalties"],
 d:"Sets how and when invoices are raised and paid, and what happens if payment is late or disputed.",
 n:"If a contract has no substantial remedy for late payment, the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998 implies interest at 8% above the Bank of England base rate.",
 o:[
 ["60 days, withholding and set-off",-2,["{S} shall invoice {B} monthly in arrears for the Charges due in respect of the preceding month.","{B} shall pay each valid and properly rendered invoice within sixty (60) days of its receipt.","{B} may withhold payment of any amount which it disputes in good faith, pending resolution of the dispute.","{B} may set off any amount owed to it by {S} against any amount payable by it to {S}."],
  "You keep your cash longer and have leverage if things go wrong.","Slow cashflow, and payment can be held up by any dispute or cross-claim."],
 ["30 days, disputes notified",0,["{S} shall invoice {B} monthly in arrears for the Charges due in respect of the preceding month.","{B} shall pay each valid invoice within thirty (30) days of its receipt, save for any amount disputed in good faith which {B} notifies to {S}, with reasons, within ten (10) Business Days of receipt. {B} shall pay the undisputed balance in accordance with this clause.","Interest shall accrue on any overdue amount at two per cent (2%) a year above the Bank of England base rate from time to time, from the due date until the date of actual payment."],
  "A standard timescale, and you can hold back genuinely disputed sums if you raise them promptly.","Fair terms, and the notice requirement stops late or tactical disputes."],
 ["In advance, no set-off",1,["{S} shall invoice {B} monthly in advance.","{B} shall pay each invoice within thirty (30) days of the date of the invoice. All amounts due under this Agreement shall be paid in full without any set-off, counterclaim, deduction or withholding, other than any deduction required by law.","Interest shall accrue on any overdue amount at four per cent (4%) a year above the Bank of England base rate from time to time, accruing daily from the due date until payment, whether before or after judgment."],
  "You pay before the work is done, and you cannot hold back money even when you have a claim.","Firm terms and compensation for late payment."],
 ["Annually in advance, suspension",2,["The Charges are payable annually in advance. {S} shall invoice {B} on the Effective Date and on each anniversary of it.","{B} shall pay each invoice within fourteen (14) days of the date of the invoice, without any set-off, counterclaim, deduction or withholding.","If any amount remains unpaid seven (7) days after its due date, {S} may, without liability, suspend performance of all or any of its obligations until payment is made in full."],
  "You pay a year up front and can be cut off within days of a late payment.","The best possible cashflow and strong leverage."]]},

"war-s":{t:"Warranties",g:["warranties"],
 d:"The promises the supplier makes about how the services will be performed and what will be delivered.",
 n:"Section 13 of the Supply of Goods and Services Act 1982 implies a term that a business supplier will use reasonable care and skill. Between businesses it can be excluded only if the exclusion is reasonable.",
 df:{"Good Industry Practice":GIP_DEF},
 o:[
 ["Enhanced standard",-2,[["{S} warrants and undertakes that:",["it shall perform the Services with the highest level of skill, care and diligence and in accordance with Good Industry Practice;","the Deliverables shall conform with the Specification and be fit for any purpose expressly or impliedly made known to {S};","the Services and the Deliverables shall comply with all applicable laws; and","all personnel used to perform the Services shall be suitably skilled, experienced and qualified."]],"If {S} breaches clause {N}.1, {S} shall, at {B}'s option and without prejudice to any other right or remedy of {B}, promptly re-perform the relevant Services or refund the Charges paid for them."],
  "Wide promises, and you choose the remedy.","The highest level of skill is a tougher standard than the law implies, and fitness for purpose can make you liable even where you were careful."],
 ["Reasonable skill and care",0,[["{S} warrants that:",["it shall perform the Services with reasonable skill and care and in accordance with Good Industry Practice; and","the Deliverables shall conform in all material respects with the Specification for ninety (90) days from their acceptance."]],"{S} shall, at its own cost, promptly re-perform any Services, or correct any Deliverables, which {B} notifies to {S} as not complying with clause {N}.1 within ninety (90) days of their performance or acceptance."],
  "The market position. A measurable standard with a clear fix.","A standard you can plan around, with a defined warranty period."],
 ["Statutory standard only",2,["{S} shall perform the Services with reasonable skill and care.","Except as expressly set out in this Agreement, all warranties, conditions and other terms implied by statute or common law, including those implied by sections 13 to 16 of the Supply of Goods and Services Act 1982, are excluded to the fullest extent permitted by law."],
  "Thin protection, and no warranty that the Deliverables will actually work.","Minimal exposure, provided a court accepts the exclusion as reasonable."]]},

war:{t:"Warranties",g:["warranties"],
 d:"The promises the seller makes about the quality of what is supplied, and the remedy if it is faulty.",
 n:"Sections 13 to 15 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 imply terms about description, quality and fitness for purpose. Between businesses these can be excluded only if reasonable, and the implied term as to title (s.12) can never be excluded.",
 o:[
 ["Full warranties, 24 months",-2,[["{S} warrants that, for twenty-four (24) months from the date of delivery, {D} shall:",["conform in all respects with their description and the Specification;","be of satisfactory quality within the meaning of the Sale of Goods Act 1979;","be fit for any purpose held out by {S} or made known to {S} by {B} before the relevant order;","be free from defects in design, materials and workmanship; and","comply with all applicable laws."]],"If any of {D} do not comply with clause {N}.1, {B} may, without prejudice to its other rights and remedies, reject them and require {S}, at {B}'s option, to repair or replace them, or to refund the price paid for them, in each case at {S}'s cost."],
  "Wide promises over a long period, and you choose the remedy.","You carry the risk of faults for two years, including fitness for purposes you may not control."],
 ["Specification, 12 months",0,["{S} warrants that, for twelve (12) months from the date of delivery, {D} shall conform in all material respects with the Specification and be free from material defects in design, materials and workmanship.","If {B} notifies {S} in writing of a breach of clause {N}.1 within that period, {S} shall, at its option, repair or replace the defective items, or refund the price paid for them.","{S} shall not be liable for any defect arising from fair wear and tear, wilful damage, negligence, abnormal storage or working conditions, or failure to follow {S}'s written instructions."],
  "The market position. Clear cover for a year, with sensible exclusions.","A fair, measurable standard, and you choose the cheapest fix."],
 ["90 days, sole remedy",1,["{S} warrants that, for ninety (90) days from the date of delivery, {D} shall conform in all material respects with the Specification.","{S}'s only obligation, and {B}'s sole remedy, for breach of clause {N}.1 shall be, at {S}'s option, to repair or replace the defective items or to refund the price paid for them.","Except as set out in this clause, all warranties, conditions and other terms implied by statute or common law, including the terms implied by sections 13 to 15 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979, are excluded to the fullest extent permitted by law."],
  "Short cover, and you cannot claim the wider losses a fault causes.","Limited exposure, and you decide how faults are fixed."],
 ["Supplied as is",2,["{D} are supplied as is. All warranties, conditions and other terms implied by statute or common law are excluded to the fullest extent permitted by law."],
  "No promises at all. You carry the whole risk of defects.","Minimal risk, though a court may disapply the exclusion if it is unreasonable."]]},

fm:{t:"Force Majeure",g:["force-majeure"],
 d:"Excuses a party from performing when events outside its control get in the way, and says what happens if they last.",
 n:"English law has no general doctrine of force majeure. Relief exists only if the contract provides it, and the separate doctrine of frustration applies only in extreme cases. A duty to overcome force majeure does not require a party to accept performance other than as the contract provides (RTI v MUR Shipping [2024] UKSC 18).",
 df:{"Good Industry Practice":GIP_DEF},
 o:[
 ["Narrow, with early exit",-2,[["In this clause, “Force Majeure Event” means an event or circumstance beyond the reasonable control of the affected party, the effects of which could not have been prevented or avoided by the exercise of Good Industry Practice, but excluding:",["any industrial action involving the workforce of the affected party or of any of its subcontractors;","any failure or delay of a subcontractor or supplier, unless itself caused by a Force Majeure Event; and","any event whose effects would have been prevented or mitigated by a business continuity plan prepared in accordance with Good Industry Practice."]],"Provided it complies with clause {N}.3, a party shall not be in breach of this Agreement to the extent its performance is prevented or delayed by a Force Majeure Event. {B} shall not be liable to pay for anything which, as a result, is not provided.","The affected party shall notify the other party within two (2) Business Days of becoming aware of the Force Majeure Event and shall use all reasonable endeavours to mitigate its effect.","If a Force Majeure Event prevents or delays {S}'s performance for more than thirty (30) days, {B} may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice."],
  "Few excuses for non-performance, you stop paying for what you do not receive, and you can leave quickly.","Supply chain and workforce problems stay with you, and the customer can walk away after a month."],
 ["Market standard, mutual",0,[["In this clause, “Force Majeure Event” means any event or circumstance beyond a party's reasonable control, including:",["acts of God, flood, drought, earthquake or other natural disaster;","epidemic or pandemic;","terrorist attack, civil war, civil commotion or riot, war or armed conflict;","nuclear, chemical or biological contamination; and","any law or action taken by a government or public authority."]],"Neither party shall be in breach of this Agreement, nor liable for any delay or failure in performing its obligations, to the extent such delay or failure results from a Force Majeure Event, provided that it promptly notifies the other party and uses all reasonable endeavours to mitigate the effect of the Force Majeure Event.","If a Force Majeure Event prevents a party from performing all or a material part of its obligations for more than ninety (90) days, either party may terminate this Agreement by giving written notice to the other."],
  "The market position. Balanced relief with a duty to work around problems.","Fair relief for events genuinely beyond your control."],
 ["Broad, no exit",2,["In this clause, “Force Majeure Event” means any cause beyond {S}'s reasonable control, including acts of God, natural disaster, epidemic or pandemic, war, terrorism, riot, any law or action of a government or public authority, any shortage of labour, materials or energy, any increase in costs, any failure of a utility, transport or telecommunications network, any cyber attack and any failure or delay of a subcontractor or supplier.","{S} shall not be liable for any delay or failure to perform its obligations resulting from a Force Majeure Event, and the time for performance shall be extended by a period equivalent to that during which performance is prevented."],
  "The other side has many excuses, and you cannot leave however long it lasts.","Wide protection for a long list of everyday business problems."]]},

ip:{t:"Intellectual Property",g:["ip"],
 d:"Decides who owns the intellectual property in the work produced, and what each side may do with it.",
 n:"Copyright in work created by an independent contractor stays with the contractor unless assigned. An assignment of copyright must be in writing and signed by the assignor (Copyright, Designs and Patents Act 1988, s.90(3)), and moral rights can be waived but not assigned (s.87).",
 df:{"Intellectual Property Rights":IPR_DEF},
 o:[
 ["{B} owns everything",-2,["{S} assigns to {B}, with full title guarantee and free from all third-party rights, by way of present assignment of present and future rights, all Intellectual Property Rights in the Deliverables, with effect from their creation.","{S} shall procure the irrevocable and unconditional waiver of all moral rights in the Deliverables to which any individual is or may be entitled.","{S} shall, at {B}'s request, promptly execute all documents and do all things reasonably required to secure and perfect {B}'s rights under this clause."],
  "You own what you paid for and can use, adapt or sell it without restriction.","You may give away rights in your own tools and methods if they end up in the work."],
 ["{B} owns bespoke, {S} keeps background",0,["{S} assigns to {B}, with full title guarantee, by way of present assignment of present and future rights, all Intellectual Property Rights in the Deliverables, excluding {S}'s Background IPR.","{S} grants to {B} a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence, with the right to sub-license to members of {B}'s group and its contractors, to use, copy and modify any of {S}'s Background IPR incorporated in the Deliverables, for the purpose of receiving and using the Services and the Deliverables.","Each party shall retain ownership of its Background IPR."],
  "The market position. You own what was made for you and can keep using everything it relies on.","You keep your core tools and can reuse them for other clients.",{"Background IPR":"Intellectual Property Rights owned by or licensed to a party before the Effective Date, or developed independently of this Agreement"}],
 ["{S} owns, perpetual licence",1,["All Intellectual Property Rights in the Deliverables shall vest in and remain with {S}.","{S} grants to {B} a perpetual, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free licence to use the Deliverables for its internal business purposes."],
  "You can use the work forever, but cannot sell it, transfer it or stop competitors getting the same thing.","You keep ownership and can reuse the work across your business."],
 ["{S} owns, licence ends",2,["All Intellectual Property Rights in the Deliverables shall vest in and remain with {S}.","{S} grants to {B} a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the Deliverables for its internal business purposes during the term of this Agreement. The licence shall terminate automatically on the termination or expiry of this Agreement.","Nothing in this Agreement restricts {S} from using the Deliverables, or any know-how gained in performing the Services, for any other purpose."],
  "You could lose the right to use work you paid for when the contract ends.","Full ownership, and strong leverage to keep the customer renewing."]]},

conf:{t:"Confidentiality",g:["confidentiality"],
 d:"Controls how each party may use and share the other's confidential information, and for how long.",
 df:{"Confidential Information":"all information of a confidential nature relating to the business, affairs, customers, clients or suppliers of a party or of any member of its group, disclosed to the other party in connection with this Agreement, other than information which is or becomes public (other than through a breach of this Agreement), was lawfully in the recipient's possession before disclosure, or is independently developed by the recipient"},
 o:[
 ["One-way, without time limit",-2,["{S} shall keep the Confidential Information of {B} confidential, shall use it only to perform its obligations under this Agreement, and shall not disclose it to any person other than those of its employees and professional advisers who need to know it for that purpose and who are bound by equivalent obligations of confidence.","The obligations in this clause shall survive termination or expiry of this Agreement without limit in time."],
  "Your information is protected for good, with nothing owed in return.","You carry the obligations alone and indefinitely."],
 ["Mutual, five years",0,["Each party shall keep the Confidential Information of the other party confidential and shall not use it for any purpose other than to exercise its rights and perform its obligations under this Agreement.",["Each party may disclose the other party's Confidential Information:",["to its employees, officers, representatives, subcontractors and advisers who need to know it for the purpose in clause {N}.1, provided that it ensures they comply with this clause as if they were a party; and","as required by law, a court of competent jurisdiction or any governmental or regulatory authority."]],"This clause shall survive termination or expiry of this Agreement for five (5) years."],
  "The market position. Balanced and long-lasting.","Fair and mutual, with a clear end date."],
 ["Mutual, marked information, two years",1,["Each party shall keep confidential any information of the other party which is marked as confidential at the time of its disclosure, and shall not disclose it to any third party save as required by law.","This clause shall survive termination or expiry of this Agreement for two (2) years."],
  "Anything you forget to mark is unprotected, and protection ends soon after the contract.","Simple to manage and short-lived."]]},

asg:{t:"Assignment and Subcontracting",g:["boilerplate"],
 d:"Says whether a party can transfer the contract, or hand the work to someone else.",
 n:"An assignment transfers only the benefit of a contract. Transferring the burden needs a novation, which requires the other party's agreement in any event.",
 o:[
 ["{B} free, {S} restricted",-2,["{B} may assign, novate or otherwise transfer any or all of its rights and obligations under this Agreement to any member of its group, or to any purchaser of all or part of its business, on written notice to {S}.","{S} shall not assign, novate, subcontract or otherwise transfer any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement without {B}'s prior written consent. {S} shall remain responsible for the acts and omissions of its subcontractors as if they were its own.","{B} may terminate this Agreement by written notice if {S} undergoes a change of control within the meaning of section 1124 of the Corporation Tax Act 2010."],
  "You can restructure or sell freely, control who does the work, and leave if the supplier changes hands.","You cannot sell your business or outsource without the customer's permission."],
 ["Mutual consent, group transfers allowed",0,["Neither party shall assign, novate or otherwise transfer any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other party, such consent not to be unreasonably withheld or delayed.","Either party may assign this Agreement to a member of its group on written notice to the other, provided that the assignee shall assign it back before ceasing to be a member of that group."],
  "The market position. Balanced, with group reorganisations allowed.","Balanced, and consent cannot be refused without a good reason."],
 ["{S} free, {B} restricted",2,["{S} may at any time assign, novate, subcontract or deal in any other manner with any or all of its rights and obligations under this Agreement.","{B} shall not assign, novate or otherwise transfer any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement without {S}'s prior written consent."],
  "Someone you did not choose could end up performing the contract.","Maximum freedom to restructure, sell or outsource."]]},

gl:{t:"Governing Law and Jurisdiction",g:["disputes"],
 d:"Chooses English law and decides where any dispute will be heard.",
 n:"English judgments can be enforced in many countries under the Hague Choice of Court Convention 2005 and, since 1 July 2025, the Hague Judgments Convention 2019. Arbitral awards are enforceable in over 170 states under the New York Convention. Since the Arbitration Act 2025, the law of the seat governs the arbitration agreement unless the parties expressly choose otherwise.",
 o:[
 ["Asymmetric, in favour of {B}",-2,["This Agreement and any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of England and Wales.","{S} irrevocably agrees that the courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any such dispute or claim. This clause is for the benefit of {B} only, which may bring proceedings in any other court of competent jurisdiction, including concurrently in more than one jurisdiction."],
  "The other side can only sue you in England, while you can sue wherever its assets are.","You are confined to the English courts while the other side chooses any forum."],
 ["English courts, exclusive",0,["This Agreement and any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of England and Wales.","Each party irrevocably agrees that the courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any such dispute or claim."],
  "The market position for UK parties. Certain, familiar and enforceable under the Hague Conventions.","Neutral and predictable for both sides."],
 ["London arbitration",0,["This Agreement and any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of England and Wales.","Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement, including any question regarding its existence, validity or termination, shall be referred to and finally resolved by arbitration under the LCIA Rules, which are deemed incorporated by reference into this clause. The number of arbitrators shall be one. The seat of the arbitration shall be London. The language of the arbitration shall be English."],
  "Private and enforceable almost anywhere. Worth it where the other side is overseas.","Private, with an award you can enforce internationally."],
 ["Asymmetric, in favour of {S}",2,["This Agreement and any dispute or claim (including non-contractual disputes or claims) arising out of or in connection with it or its subject matter or formation shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of England and Wales.","{B} irrevocably agrees that the courts of England and Wales shall have exclusive jurisdiction to settle any such dispute or claim. This clause is for the benefit of {S} only, which may bring proceedings in any other court of competent jurisdiction, including concurrently in more than one jurisdiction."],
  "You are confined to the English courts while the other side chooses any forum.","You can pursue the other side wherever its assets are, while it can only sue you in England."]]},

dr:{t:"Dispute Resolution",g:["disputes"],
 d:"Sets the steps the parties must take to try to settle a dispute before going to court.",
 n:"English courts can order parties to engage in mediation or other dispute resolution (Churchill v Merthyr Tydfil County Borough Council [2023] EWCA Civ 1416), so a clear contractual procedure is valuable.",
 o:[
 ["Direct access to court",-1,["No dispute resolution procedure shall be a condition precedent to the commencement of proceedings, and nothing in this Agreement shall prevent either party from commencing proceedings at any time or from seeking urgent injunctive or other interim relief."],
  "You can act quickly when you need a remedy.","You may face proceedings before any chance to settle."],
 ["Escalation, then mediation",0,["If any dispute arises in connection with this Agreement, either party may refer it by written notice to the senior executives of each party, who shall meet within ten (10) Business Days of the notice to attempt to resolve it in good faith.","If the dispute is not resolved within twenty (20) Business Days of that notice, the parties shall attempt to settle it by mediation in accordance with the CEDR Model Mediation Procedure.","If the dispute is not resolved within forty-five (45) days of the initial notice, either party may commence proceedings. Nothing in this clause shall prevent either party from seeking urgent interim relief."],
  "The market position. A short, structured route to settlement before court.","Time and a process to settle disputes commercially."],
 ["Mandatory extended process",1,[["No party may commence any court proceedings or arbitration in relation to any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement until:",["the dispute has been the subject of negotiation between the senior executives of each party for not less than sixty (60) days; and","a mediation has taken place in accordance with the CEDR Model Mediation Procedure and has failed to resolve the dispute."]],"Nothing in this clause shall prevent a party from seeking urgent interim relief."],
  "Your claims could be delayed for months.","Strong pressure to settle, and time to put problems right."]]},

dp:{t:"Data Protection",g:["data"],
 d:"The terms on which one party processes personal data on behalf of the other.",
 n:"Article 28(3) of the UK GDPR lists terms that must be in every controller to processor contract. A promise simply to comply with the law does not satisfy it. The UK regime has been amended by the Data (Use and Access) Act 2025.",
 df:{"UK GDPR":"has the meaning given to it in section 3(10), as supplemented by section 205(4), of the Data Protection Act 2018","Personal Data":"has the meaning given to it in the UK GDPR","Personal Data Breach":"has the meaning given to it in the UK GDPR"},
 o:[
 ["Strict processor terms",-2,[["{S} shall, in relation to any Personal Data processed on behalf of {B} under this Agreement:",["process that Personal Data only on the documented instructions of {B}, unless required to do otherwise by law;","ensure that all persons authorised to process the Personal Data are subject to a binding duty of confidentiality;","implement the technical and organisational measures set out in {SC:sec}, and any further measures required to comply with Article 32 of the UK GDPR;","not engage any sub-processor without {B}'s prior specific written consent;","assist {B} in responding to requests from data subjects and in complying with its obligations under Articles 32 to 36 of the UK GDPR;","notify {B} without undue delay, and in any event within twenty-four (24) hours, after becoming aware of a Personal Data Breach;","at {B}'s choice, delete or return all the Personal Data when the processing under this Agreement ends; and","make available to {B} all information necessary to demonstrate compliance with this clause, and allow for and contribute to audits and inspections conducted by {B} or its auditor on reasonable notice."]],"{S}'s liability for breach of this clause shall not be subject to any limitation of liability in this Agreement."],
  "Tight control of your data, rapid warning of any breach and uncapped recovery.","Heavy obligations, and unlimited exposure if anything goes wrong."],
 ["Article 28 standard",0,[["{S} shall, in relation to any Personal Data processed on behalf of {B} under this Agreement:",["process that Personal Data only on the documented instructions of {B}, unless required to do otherwise by law;","ensure that all persons authorised to process the Personal Data are subject to a binding duty of confidentiality;","implement appropriate technical and organisational measures in accordance with Article 32 of the UK GDPR;","not engage any sub-processor without {B}'s prior general written authorisation, and give {B} not less than thirty (30) days' notice of any intended addition or replacement, during which {B} may object on reasonable grounds;","assist {B} in responding to requests from data subjects and in complying with its obligations under Articles 32 to 36 of the UK GDPR;","notify {B} without undue delay, and in any event within forty-eight (48) hours, after becoming aware of a Personal Data Breach;","at {B}'s choice, delete or return all the Personal Data when the processing under this Agreement ends; and","make available to {B} the information necessary to demonstrate compliance with this clause, and allow for audits not more than once in any twelve (12) month period, on not less than thirty (30) days' notice and during normal business hours."]]],
  "The market position. Meets the legal requirements with workable controls.","Compliant and practical to operate."],
 ["Compliance and certificates",2,["{S} shall comply with its obligations under the Data Protection Legislation to the extent applicable to its processing of Personal Data under this Agreement.","{S} shall notify {B} without undue delay after becoming aware of a Personal Data Breach.","Any right of {B} to audit or inspect {S} shall be satisfied in full by {S} providing a copy of its current ISO/IEC 27001 certificate or SOC 2 Type II report."],
  "Too thin. It does not contain the Article 28 terms, so as controller you are exposed to the regulator.","Low burden, but it is non-compliant and is likely to be rejected by any well-advised customer.",{"Data Protection Legislation":"the UK GDPR, the Data Protection Act 2018 and all other legislation relating to the processing of personal data that applies in the United Kingdom, in each case as amended from time to time"}]]},

sla:{t:"Service Levels",g:["penalties"],
 d:"Sets the promised availability of the service, and what the customer receives when it is missed.",
 n:"Describing service credits as a price adjustment rather than compensation reflects their purpose and helps preserve the customer's other remedies.",
 df:{"Available":"the Service is accessible and materially functional for use by the Authorised Users in accordance with the Documentation, and “Availability” shall be construed accordingly","Scheduled Maintenance":"maintenance of the Service notified to {B} at least five (5) Business Days in advance and carried out outside the hours of 8.00 am to 6.00 pm on Business Days","Service Credits":"the credits against the Charges calculated in accordance with {SC:credits}"},
 o:[
 ["99.95%, credits not sole remedy",-2,["{S} shall ensure that the Service is Available for at least 99.95% of each calendar month, excluding Scheduled Maintenance.","If Availability in any calendar month falls below that level, {S} shall credit {B} with Service Credits, up to a maximum of thirty per cent (30%) of the Charges for that month.","Service Credits are a price adjustment reflecting the reduced value of the Service and are without prejudice to {B}'s right to claim damages or to exercise any other right or remedy.","{B} may terminate this Agreement immediately by written notice if Availability falls below 99.5% in any three (3) calendar months within any rolling period of six (6) months."],
  "Very high reliability, meaningful credits, and you keep the right to sue and to leave.","Hard to achieve, and the credits are only the start of your exposure."],
 ["99.9%, credits with chronic failure exit",0,["{S} shall ensure that the Service is Available for at least 99.9% of each calendar month, excluding Scheduled Maintenance.","If Availability in any calendar month falls below that level, {S} shall credit {B} with Service Credits, up to a maximum of fifteen per cent (15%) of the Charges for that month.","Service Credits shall be {B}'s sole financial remedy for any failure to meet the availability target, without prejudice to {B}'s right to terminate this Agreement for material breach or following a Chronic Failure.","{B} may terminate this Agreement by written notice within thirty (30) days after any Chronic Failure."],
  "The market position. Fair compensation and a way out if problems persist.","A common, achievable target with predictable exposure.",{"Chronic Failure":"Availability of less than 99.0% in any two (2) consecutive calendar months"}],
 ["99.5%, reasonable endeavours",1,["{S} shall use reasonable endeavours to make the Service Available for 99.5% of each calendar month, excluding Scheduled Maintenance and any unavailability caused by circumstances beyond {S}'s reasonable control.","If Availability in any calendar month falls below that level and {B} claims within thirty (30) days after the end of that month, {S} shall credit {B} with Service Credits, up to a maximum of ten per cent (10%) of the Charges for that month. Service Credits shall be {B}'s sole and exclusive remedy for any failure to make the Service Available."],
  "Up to about 3.6 hours of downtime a month is allowed, the credits are small, and they are your only remedy.","A soft obligation with low, capped exposure."],
 ["No commitment",2,["{S} shall use commercially reasonable efforts to make the Service available. {S} does not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free, and no Service Credits or other remedy shall apply in respect of any unavailability."],
  "No measurable promise and nothing back when the service fails.","No performance risk at all."]]},

susp:{t:"Suspension",g:["termination"],
 d:"Says when the supplier can switch the service off.",
 o:[
 ["Only where required by law",-2,["{S} may suspend the Service only to the extent and for so long as it is required to do so by law or by order of a competent authority, and shall give {B} as much prior notice of the suspension as is lawful."],
  "Your service stays on while any dispute is resolved.","You lose your main leverage over unpaid invoices."],
 ["Non-payment, after warning",0,["If any undisputed amount remains unpaid for more than thirty (30) days after its due date, {S} may give {B} written notice of its intention to suspend the Service. If payment is not received within fourteen (14) days of that notice, {S} may suspend the Service until payment is made in full.","{S} may also suspend the Service, to the minimum extent necessary, where this is required to prevent a serious threat to the security or integrity of the Service, and shall notify {B} promptly."],
  "The market position. Fair warning before anything is switched off.","A clear and usable remedy for non-payment and security threats."],
 ["Immediate, on wide grounds",2,[["{S} may suspend all or any part of the Service immediately and without notice if:",["any amount due to {S} is unpaid;","{S} reasonably suspects that {B} or any Authorised User has breached this Agreement or the Acceptable Use Policy; or","{S} considers suspension necessary to protect the Service or any of its other customers."]],"The Charges shall continue to accrue during any period of suspension."],
  "Your business could stop overnight on a suspicion, and you keep paying.","Maximum leverage and protection for your platform.",{"Acceptable Use Policy":"{S}'s acceptable use policy for the Service, as published by {S} from time to time"}]]},

exit:{t:"Exit and Return of Data",g:["data"],
 d:"What happens to the customer's data, and what help the customer gets, when the contract ends.",
 n:"Where personal data is involved, Article 28(3)(g) UK GDPR requires the processor to delete or return it at the controller's choice at the end of the services.",
 df:{"Customer Data":"all data, including Personal Data, supplied by or on behalf of {B}, or generated by {S} on {B}'s behalf, under this Agreement"},
 o:[
 ["Free return and exit support",-2,[["On termination or expiry of this Agreement for any reason, {S} shall, at no additional charge:",["return all Customer Data to {B} within thirty (30) days in such industry-standard format as {B} reasonably requests; and","on {B}'s written instruction, securely delete all copies of the Customer Data in its possession or control and certify in writing that it has done so."]],"For up to six (6) months after termination or expiry, {S} shall provide such assistance as {B} reasonably requests to enable an orderly transfer of the Services to {B} or a replacement supplier, at the rates set out in this Agreement."],
  "A smooth move to a new provider, and your data can never be held hostage.","Unpaid work and continuing effort for a customer you are losing."],
 ["Thirty-day export window",0,["For thirty (30) days after termination or expiry of this Agreement, {S} shall make the Customer Data available to {B} for download in {S}'s standard export format.","After that period, {S} shall delete the Customer Data, save to the extent that it is required by law to retain it."],
  "The market position. Workable, but you must plan the migration in advance.","Simple and inexpensive to provide."],
 ["Deletion after seven days",2,["{S} may delete all Customer Data in its possession or control at any time after the seventh (7th) day following termination or expiry of this Agreement.","Any return of Customer Data or exit assistance requested by {B} shall be provided at {S}'s then-current professional services rates, subject to payment of all outstanding Charges."],
  "Real risk of losing data and paying heavily for help, and likely non-compliant for personal data.","Little ongoing cost, and leverage at renewal."]]},

price:{t:"Changes to the Charges",g:["penalties"],
 d:"Controls whether, when and by how much the charges can increase.",
 df:{"CPI":"the Consumer Prices Index (all items) published by the Office for National Statistics, or any replacement index"},
 o:[
 ["Fixed, then capped",-2,["The Charges shall remain fixed for the Initial Term.","After the Initial Term, {S} may increase the Charges no more than once in any Contract Year, by giving not less than ninety (90) days' written notice, by a percentage not exceeding the lower of the percentage increase in CPI over the preceding twelve (12) months and three per cent (3%)."],
  "Budget certainty for years.","Inflation and rising costs eat into your margin.",{"Contract Year":"each period of twelve (12) months beginning on the Effective Date or on any anniversary of it"}],
 ["Annual CPI",0,["{S} may, by giving not less than sixty (60) days' written notice, increase the Charges with effect from each anniversary of the Effective Date by a percentage not exceeding the percentage increase in CPI over the preceding twelve (12) months."],
  "The market position. Increases track inflation and are predictable.","You keep pace with inflation."],
 ["Uncapped, with an exit",1,["{S} may increase the Charges by giving not less than sixty (60) days' written notice.","If any increase exceeds five per cent (5%), {B} may terminate this Agreement by giving written notice before the increase takes effect."],
  "Prices can jump, and leaving may be impractical once you rely on the service.","Pricing freedom, with only a limited risk of losing the customer."],
 ["At any time",2,["{S} may vary the Charges at any time by giving {B} not less than thirty (30) days' written notice."],
  "No price certainty at all.","Complete pricing freedom."]]},

"dev-acc":{t:"Acceptance",g:["warranties"],
 d:"How the customer tests the work and confirms it is complete, and what happens if it fails.",
 df:{"Acceptance Criteria":"the acceptance criteria for each Deliverable set out in the relevant Statement of Work"},
 o:[
 ["Customer-led, refund on failure",-2,["On delivery of each Deliverable, {B} shall carry out acceptance tests to determine whether it meets the Acceptance Criteria.","If a Deliverable fails its acceptance tests, {S} shall remedy the failure and re-deliver the Deliverable within ten (10) Business Days. If the Deliverable fails its acceptance tests on a third occasion, {B} may reject it and terminate this Agreement, in which case {S} shall refund all Charges paid under this Agreement within thirty (30) days.","A Deliverable shall be accepted only when {B} issues a written acceptance certificate in respect of it."],
  "You only pay for software that works, and you control sign-off.","Real risk of doing the work and being paid nothing."],
 ["Agreed tests, deemed acceptance",0,["{S} shall notify {B} when each Deliverable is ready for testing, and the parties shall carry out the tests set out in the Test Plan within ten (10) Business Days of that notice.","If a Deliverable fails to meet the Acceptance Criteria, {S} shall correct it and re-submit it for testing. If it fails a second re-test, {B} may accept it subject to a reasonable reduction in the Charges, or reject it and recover the Charges paid for it.","A Deliverable shall be deemed accepted if {B} does not notify {S} of a material failure within the testing period, or if {B} uses it in a live environment other than for testing."],
  "The market position. A fair process with fixed deadlines.","A clear route to sign-off and payment.",{"Test Plan":"the plan for the acceptance testing of the Deliverables agreed by the parties in writing"}],
 ["Accepted on delivery or use",2,[["Each Deliverable shall be deemed accepted on the earlier of:",["the date of its delivery; and","the date on which {B} first uses it in a live environment."]],"{S}'s only obligation in respect of any defect notified after acceptance shall be to use reasonable endeavours to correct it under the warranty in this Agreement."],
  "No proper chance to test before you are committed.","Quick sign-off and payment."]]},

"gd-title":{t:"Risk and Title",g:["warranties"],
 d:"When ownership of the goods, and the risk of their loss or damage, passes to the buyer.",
 n:"Retention of title is effective under English law if properly drafted, but claims over goods that have been mixed with others or processed usually fail, and may take effect as an unregistered charge.",
 o:[
 ["Title early, risk late",-2,["Title to {D} shall pass to {B} on the earlier of their delivery and payment for them.","Risk in {D} shall remain with {S} until {D} have been delivered to and accepted by {B}. {B} shall be deemed to have accepted {D} if it does not notify {S} of any defect within thirty (30) days after delivery."],
  "You own the goods early and carry no risk until you have accepted them.","You carry the risk until acceptance and lose your security for payment."],
 ["Risk on delivery, title on payment",0,["Risk in {D} shall pass to {B} on completion of delivery.","Title to {D} shall not pass to {B} until {S} has received payment in full for them.","Until title passes, {B} shall hold {D} as {S}'s bailee, store them separately and keep them identifiable as {S}'s property, but may resell or use them in the ordinary course of its business."],
  "The market position. Insure the goods from delivery.","You keep security over the goods until you are paid."],
 ["All-monies retention, ex works",2,["Risk in {D} shall pass to {B} when {D} are made available for collection at {S}'s premises, notwithstanding any arrangement for {S} to arrange their delivery.","Title to {D} shall not pass to {B} until {S} has received payment in full, in cleared funds, of all sums due to it from {B} on any account.","Until title passes, {B} shall hold {D} as {S}'s bailee, and {S} may at any time require {B} to deliver up {D} and, if {B} fails to do so, enter any premises where {D} are stored in order to recover them."],
  "You carry the risk in transit and may not own goods you have already paid for.","Strong security for every debt, and no risk in transit."]]},

"dist-excl":{t:"Appointment",g:["competition"],
 d:"Appoints the distributor and decides whether it is the only one allowed to sell in its territory.",
 n:"Territorial restrictions are governed by the Competition Act 1998 (Vertical Agreements Block Exemption) Order 2022. Restricting a distributor's passive sales is generally not permitted.",
 o:[
 ["Exclusive, no targets",-2,["{S} appoints {B} as its exclusive distributor of the Products in the Territory for the term of this Agreement.",["During the term of this Agreement, {S} shall not:",["appoint any other person to distribute or sell the Products in the Territory; or","itself sell the Products to customers in the Territory."]],"{B} shall not be subject to any minimum purchase obligation."],
  "The territory is yours, with no pressure to perform.","Your only route to that market, and no way to make it perform."],
 ["Exclusive, subject to targets",0,["{S} appoints {B} as its exclusive distributor of the Products in the Territory for the term of this Agreement, and shall not appoint any other distributor in the Territory.","If, in any Contract Year, {B} fails to purchase Products to the value of the Minimum Purchase Target for that year, {S} may, by giving thirty (30) days' written notice within three (3) months after the end of that year, convert the appointment to a non-exclusive appointment."],
  "The market position. You keep exclusivity by performing.","You can open the market if sales fall short.",{"Minimum Purchase Target":"the minimum purchase target for each Contract Year set out in {SC:targets}","Contract Year":"each period of twelve (12) months beginning on the Effective Date or on any anniversary of it"}],
 ["Non-exclusive",2,["{S} appoints {B} as its non-exclusive distributor of the Products in the Territory.","{S} reserves the right to appoint other distributors, agents or resellers in the Territory, and to sell the Products directly to any customer in the Territory."],
  "Others can undercut you in your own territory.","Full flexibility in how you reach the market."]]},

"agency-comp":{t:"Indemnity or Compensation on Termination",g:["termination"],
 d:"What the agent is entitled to receive when the agency ends.",
 n:"Under regulation 17 of the Commercial Agents (Council Directive) Regulations 1993, an agent is entitled to compensation on termination unless the contract provides for an indemnity instead. An indemnity is capped at one year's average remuneration (reg. 17(4)). These rights cannot be excluded to the agent's detriment before the contract ends (reg. 19).",
 o:[
 ["Indemnity",-1,["On termination of this Agreement, {S} shall be entitled to an indemnity in accordance with regulation 17(3) to (5) of the Regulations, and shall not be entitled to compensation under regulation 17(6)."],
  "The payout is capped at about a year's commission.","Capped, and usually less valuable than compensation."],
 ["Compensation",1,["On termination of this Agreement, {S} shall be entitled to compensation in accordance with regulation 17(6) and (7) of the Regulations.","Nothing in this Agreement shall operate to derogate from regulations 17 and 18 of the Regulations to the detriment of {S}."],
  "Uncapped. Courts value it as the price the agency would fetch on the open market.","Often the more valuable entitlement."]]},

/* ---------------- licensing ---------------- */
"lic-scope":{t:"Grant of Licence",g:["ip"],
 d:"Grants the licence and decides whether anyone else, including the licensor, may use the same rights.",
 n:"An exclusive licensee of a UK patent may sue infringers in its own name (Patents Act 1977, s.67). A sole licensee cannot.",
 df:{"Intellectual Property Rights":IPR_DEF},
 o:[
 ["Exclusive",-2,["{S} grants to {B} an exclusive licence under the Licensed IPR to make, have made, use, sell and otherwise dispose of the Licensed Products in the Field in the Territory during the Term.","During the Term, {S} shall not itself exploit, or grant any other person any right to exploit, the Licensed IPR in the Field in the Territory."],
  "No one else, not even the licensor, can use the rights in your territory.","You give up the right to exploit your own IP in that market."],
 ["Sole",0,["{S} grants to {B} a sole licence under the Licensed IPR to make, have made, use, sell and otherwise dispose of the Licensed Products in the Field in the Territory during the Term.","{S} shall not grant any other licence of the Licensed IPR in the Field in the Territory during the Term, but reserves the right to exploit the Licensed IPR itself."],
  "No competing licensees, though the licensor may still compete with you.","You keep your own right to use the IP."],
 ["Non-exclusive",2,["{S} grants to {B} a non-exclusive licence under the Licensed IPR to make, have made, use, sell and otherwise dispose of the Licensed Products in the Field in the Territory during the Term.","{S} may itself exploit, and may grant licences to others to exploit, the Licensed IPR in the Field in the Territory."],
  "Competitors may get the same rights, which may not justify your investment.","Full freedom to license as widely as you like."]]},

"lic-imp":{t:"Improvements",g:["ip","competition"],
 d:"Who owns improvements the licensee makes to the licensed technology.",
 n:"Competition law treats an obligation to assign or exclusively license severable improvements back to the licensor with suspicion. Take specific advice before using a full grant-back.",
 df:{"Improvement":"any modification, development or improvement of the Licensed IPR or the Licensed Products"},
 o:[
 ["Licensee owns, no grant-back",-2,["All Intellectual Property Rights in any Improvement made by or on behalf of {B} shall belong to {B}.","{B} shall have no obligation to disclose or license any Improvement to {S}."],
  "Your innovation stays yours.","Others improve your technology and you get no access."],
 ["Licensee owns, licence back",0,["All Intellectual Property Rights in any Improvement made by or on behalf of {B} shall belong to {B}.","{B} shall promptly disclose each Improvement to {S} and grants to {S} a non-exclusive, perpetual, royalty-free licence to use it."],
  "The market position. You keep ownership and share use.","You benefit from improvements to your technology."],
 ["Assignment to licensor",2,["{B} shall promptly disclose to {S} every Improvement made by or on behalf of {B}, and assigns to {S}, by way of present assignment of future rights, all Intellectual Property Rights in every such Improvement."],
  "You hand over your own innovation for nothing, and the clause may be unenforceable.","You capture every development, subject to competition law."]]},

"lic-war":{t:"Licensor's Warranties",g:["warranties","ip"],
 d:"The promises the licensor makes about owning, and being free to license, the rights.",
 o:[
 ["Full warranties",-2,[["{S} warrants that:",["it is the sole legal and beneficial owner of the Licensed IPR;","the Licensed IPR is valid and subsisting, and all renewal fees have been paid;","the exploitation of the Licensed IPR in accordance with this Agreement will not infringe the rights of any third party; and","no claim has been made or threatened challenging the validity or ownership of the Licensed IPR."]]],
  "You are protected if the rights turn out to be invalid or infringing.","You guarantee matters that even a careful owner cannot be sure of, such as validity."],
 ["Title and knowledge",0,[["{S} warrants that:",["it is the owner of, or otherwise entitled to license, the Licensed IPR and has the right to grant the licence in this Agreement; and","at the date of this Agreement it has not received written notice of any claim challenging the validity or ownership of the Licensed IPR or alleging that its exploitation infringes the rights of any third party."]]],
  "The market position. You know the licensor has the right to license and has disclosed known claims.","You only promise what you know."],
 ["No warranty of validity",2,["{S} gives no warranty that the Licensed IPR is valid, or that the exploitation of the Licensed IPR will not infringe the rights of any third party.","{B} acknowledges that it has relied on its own investigations in entering into this Agreement."],
  "You bear the risk that the rights are worthless or infringe someone else's.","Minimal exposure."]]},

/* ---------------- M&A ---------------- */
"ma-price":{t:"Price Adjustment",g:["price-mechanisms"],
 d:"How the final price is worked out, either by accounts drawn up after completion or fixed in advance by a locked box.",
 o:[
 ["Completion accounts, {B} prepares",-2,["Within sixty (60) Business Days after Completion, {B} shall prepare and deliver to {S} a draft of the Completion Accounts, prepared in accordance with {SC:acc}.","{S} may, within twenty (20) Business Days of receipt, notify {B} in writing of any matter in the draft it disputes, with reasons. Any matter not so notified shall be final and binding.","The Consideration shall be adjusted on a pound-for-pound basis by the amount by which Net Debt shown in the Completion Accounts differs from zero, and by the amount by which Working Capital differs from the Target Working Capital.","{B} shall be entitled to retain ten per cent (10%) of the Consideration from the payment due at Completion until the Completion Accounts have been agreed or determined."],
  "You control the numbers and only pay for what you actually receive.","Price uncertainty, and the buyer holds both the pen and part of your money.",{"Completion Accounts":"the accounts of {T} as at the Completion Date, prepared in accordance with {SC:acc}","Net Debt":"the aggregate borrowings of {T} less its cash, each as shown in the Completion Accounts","Working Capital":"the working capital of {T} as shown in the Completion Accounts","Target Working Capital":"£[●]"}],
 ["Completion accounts, {S} prepares",0,["Within sixty (60) Business Days after Completion, {S} shall prepare and deliver to {B} a draft of the Completion Accounts, prepared in accordance with {SC:acc}.","{B} may, within thirty (30) Business Days of receipt, notify {S} of any matter it disputes. Any dispute not resolved within twenty (20) Business Days shall be referred to the Independent Accountant, who shall act as an expert and not as an arbitrator, and whose determination shall be final and binding save in the case of manifest error.","The Consideration shall be adjusted on a pound-for-pound basis by the amount by which Net Debt shown in the Completion Accounts differs from zero, and by the amount by which Working Capital differs from the Target Working Capital."],
  "You still pay for the true position, with an independent expert for disputes.","You prepare the first draft and any dispute goes to an expert.",{"Completion Accounts":"the accounts of {T} as at the Completion Date, prepared in accordance with {SC:acc}","Independent Accountant":"an independent firm of chartered accountants agreed by the parties or, failing agreement, nominated by the President of the Institute of Chartered Accountants in England and Wales","Net Debt":"the aggregate borrowings of {T} less its cash, each as shown in the Completion Accounts","Working Capital":"the working capital of {T} as shown in the Completion Accounts","Target Working Capital":"£[●]"}],
 ["Locked box",1,["The Consideration has been agreed by reference to the Locked Box Accounts and shall not be subject to adjustment, save in respect of Leakage.","{S} undertakes to {B} that, in the period from the Locked Box Date to Completion, there has not been and will not be any Leakage other than Permitted Leakage.","{S} shall pay to {B} on demand an amount equal to any Leakage received by {S} or any person connected with it, provided that {B} notifies {S} in writing of the claim within six (6) months after Completion."],
  "No adjustment if trading dips after the locked box date. Your protection is the leakage covenant, so review it closely.","Price certainty at signing and no argument after completion.",{"Locked Box Accounts":"the balance sheet of {T} as at the Locked Box Date","Locked Box Date":"[●]","Leakage":"any dividend or distribution, payment to or for the benefit of {S} or any person connected with it, waiver of any amount owed by any of them, or assumption of any liability for their benefit, in each case by {T}","Permitted Leakage":"the payments listed in {SC:leak}"}],
 ["Locked box with ticker",2,["The Consideration has been agreed by reference to the Locked Box Accounts and shall not be subject to adjustment, save in respect of Leakage.","In addition, {B} shall pay to {S} at Completion an amount equal to £[●] for each day in the period from (and including) the Locked Box Date to (and including) the Completion Date.","{S} undertakes to {B} that, in the period from the Locked Box Date to Completion, there has not been any Leakage other than Permitted Leakage, and shall pay to {B} an amount equal to any Leakage actually received by {S}, provided that {B} notifies {S} of the claim within three (3) months after Completion."],
  "You pay for profits during the gap, and the leakage protection is short and has wide exceptions.","Certainty, plus compensation for the time the deal takes to close.",{"Locked Box Accounts":"the balance sheet of {T} as at the Locked Box Date","Locked Box Date":"[●]","Leakage":"any dividend or distribution, payment to or for the benefit of {S}, waiver of any amount owed by {S}, or assumption of any liability for its benefit, in each case by {T}","Permitted Leakage":"any payment made in the ordinary course of business, any payment of management or monitoring fees, and any payment made with {B}'s written consent"}]]},

"ma-mac":{t:"Conditions and Termination",g:["price-mechanisms"],
 d:"What must happen before completion, and whether the buyer can walk away if the target deteriorates.",
 n:"The National Security and Investment Act 2021 makes notification mandatory for acquisitions in 17 sensitive sectors. An acquisition completed without the required approval is void.",
 o:[
 ["Broad material adverse change",-2,["Completion is conditional on the satisfaction, or waiver by {B}, of the conditions set out in {SC:cond} (the “Conditions”), including the receipt of any approval required under the National Security and Investment Act 2021.",["{B} may terminate this Agreement by notice to {S} at any time before Completion if:",["any Warranty is or becomes untrue, inaccurate or misleading; or","any event, matter or circumstance occurs which has had, or could reasonably be expected to have, a material adverse effect on the business, operations, assets, liabilities, financial condition or prospects of {T}."]]],
  "You can walk away if the business, or the market, turns against you.","Low certainty of closing, and the buyer has an easy option to leave."],
 ["Target-specific, quantified MAC",0,["Completion is conditional on the satisfaction, or waiver by {B}, of the conditions set out in {SC:cond} (the “Conditions”), including the receipt of any approval required under the National Security and Investment Act 2021.","{B} may terminate this Agreement by notice to {S} at any time before Completion if a Material Adverse Change occurs."],
  "The market position. Protection against problems specific to the target.","Market-wide risk stays with the buyer, and the threshold is measurable.",{"Material Adverse Change":"any event or circumstance which results, or is reasonably likely to result, in a reduction in the consolidated net assets of {T} of more than [●] per cent., but excluding any event or circumstance arising from changes in general economic, political or market conditions, changes in law or accounting standards, changes generally affecting the industry in which {T} operates, or any act required by this Agreement or taken at {B}'s request"}],
 ["Regulatory conditions only",2,["Completion is conditional only on the satisfaction of the conditions set out in {SC:cond} (the “Conditions”), being the regulatory approvals required by law, including under the National Security and Investment Act 2021.","{B} shall have no right to terminate this Agreement before Completion, save where any Condition has not been satisfied by the Long Stop Date."],
  "You must complete even if the business deteriorates before closing.","Maximum certainty that the deal will close.",{"Long Stop Date":"[●], or such later date as the parties may agree in writing"}]]},

"ma-esc":{t:"Retention",g:["price-mechanisms"],
 d:"Holds back part of the price as security for claims after completion.",
 df:{"Escrow Account":"the interest-bearing account held by the Escrow Agent under the Escrow Agreement","Escrow Agreement":"the escrow agreement in the agreed form between {S}, {B} and [●] (the “Escrow Agent”)"},
 o:[
 ["15% for 24 months",-2,["At Completion, {B} shall pay an amount equal to fifteen per cent (15%) of the Consideration (the “Retention Amount”) into the Escrow Account, to be held in accordance with the Escrow Agreement.","On the date falling twenty-four (24) months after Completion, the balance of the Retention Amount shall be released to {S}, less the aggregate amount of any Claims notified by {B} and not then finally resolved, which shall be retained until their resolution."],
  "Ready money to meet claims without having to chase the seller.","A large part of your proceeds is tied up for two years."],
 ["5% for 12 months",0,["At Completion, {B} shall pay an amount equal to five per cent (5%) of the Consideration (the “Retention Amount”) into the Escrow Account, to be held in accordance with the Escrow Agreement.","On the date falling twelve (12) months after Completion, the balance of the Retention Amount shall be released to {S}, less the amount of any Claims notified by {B} and not then finally resolved."],
  "Some security for the claims most likely to arise early.","A modest retention for a short period."],
 ["No retention",2,["The Consideration shall be paid in full in cash at Completion. No part of the Consideration shall be retained or deferred as security for any Claim."],
  "If you have a claim, you must pursue the seller for the money.","You receive the whole price on completion."]]},

"ma-disc":{t:"Disclosure",g:["warranties"],
 d:"What the seller can point to in order to say the buyer was told about a problem, which stops the buyer claiming for it.",
 n:"English law has not settled whether a buyer can claim for a breach it knew about before signing (Eurocopy v Teesdale [1992] BCLC 1067; Infiniteland v Artisan [2005] EWCA Civ 758), so the agreement should deal with it expressly.",
 o:[
 ["Specific disclosure, buyer knowledge irrelevant",-2,["The Warranties are qualified only by the facts and circumstances fairly disclosed in the Disclosure Letter, with sufficient detail to enable a reasonable buyer to identify the nature and scope of the matter disclosed and to make an informed assessment of its effect.","No information of which {B} or its advisers has knowledge (actual, constructive or imputed), and no investigation by or on behalf of {B}, shall prejudice any Claim or reduce any amount recoverable.","No general disclosure in the Disclosure Letter shall qualify any Warranty."],
  "Only clear, specific disclosures reduce your rights, and you can still claim for matters you knew about.","You must disclose with precision, and the buyer can claim for things it already knew."],
 ["Fair disclosure, including the data room",0,["The Warranties are qualified by the facts and circumstances fairly disclosed in the Disclosure Letter, including the documents in the Data Room which are deemed disclosed by it.","For the purposes of this clause, “fairly disclosed” means disclosed with sufficient detail to enable a reasonable buyer to identify the nature and scope of the matter disclosed."],
  "The market position. Everything in the data room counts, so review it carefully.","The data room protects you, but only where disclosure is clear.",{"Data Room":"the virtual data room relating to {T} hosted by [●], the contents of which are listed in the index annexed to the Disclosure Letter"}],
 ["General disclosure, buyer knowledge",2,[["The Warranties are qualified by:",["all matters disclosed or referred to in the Disclosure Letter or the Data Room;","all matters which would be revealed by a search of the public registers maintained by Companies House, HM Land Registry or the Intellectual Property Office on the Business Day before the date of this Agreement; and","all matters within the actual, constructive or imputed knowledge of {B} or its advisers."]],"{B} shall not be entitled to bring any Claim in respect of any matter of which it is aware at the date of this Agreement."],
  "Anything buried in the data room, on a public register or known to your advisers defeats your claim.","Very strong protection against claims.",{"Data Room":"the virtual data room relating to {T} hosted by [●], the contents of which are listed in the index annexed to the Disclosure Letter"}]]},

"ma-wlim":{t:"Limitations on Claims",g:["warranties","liability"],
 d:"The thresholds, overall cap and time limit that apply to warranty claims against the seller.",
 n:"Thresholds and caps are expressed as percentages of the Consideration, the way deal teams negotiate them. None of these limitations applies in the case of fraud.",
 o:[
 ["Low thresholds, full cap",-2,["{S} shall not be liable for any Claim, or series of Claims arising from the same or similar facts, unless the amount of it exceeds £[●], being 0.01% of the Consideration.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim unless the aggregate amount of all Claims exceeds £[●], being 0.25% of the Consideration, in which case {S} shall be liable for the whole amount and not merely the excess.","{S}'s total liability for all Claims shall not exceed an amount equal to the Consideration.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim unless {B} has notified {S} of it, with reasonable details, before the date falling thirty-six (36) months after Completion."],
  "Almost every genuine claim can be brought and recovered in full.","Your whole sale price remains at risk for three years."],
 ["Market tipping basket",0,["{S} shall not be liable for any Claim, or series of Claims arising from the same or similar facts, unless the amount of it exceeds £[●], being 0.1% of the Consideration.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim unless the aggregate amount of all Claims exceeds £[●], being 1% of the Consideration, in which case {S} shall be liable for the whole amount and not merely the excess.","{S}'s total liability for all Claims shall not exceed fifty per cent (50%) of the Consideration.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim unless {B} has notified {S} of it, with reasonable details, before the date falling twenty-four (24) months after Completion."],
  "The market position. Small claims are filtered out but real ones are recoverable.","A familiar balance that keeps exposure proportionate."],
 ["Deductible basket, low cap",1,["{S} shall not be liable for any Claim, or series of Claims arising from the same or similar facts, unless the amount of it exceeds £[●], being 0.1% of the Consideration.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim unless the aggregate amount of all Claims exceeds £[●], being 1% of the Consideration, in which case {S} shall be liable only for the excess.","{S}'s total liability for all Claims shall not exceed twenty per cent (20%) of the Consideration.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim unless {B} has notified {S} of it, with reasonable details, before the date falling eighteen (18) months after Completion.","{S} shall not be liable for any Claim to the extent that the loss is recoverable under any policy of insurance."],
  "You bear the first 1% of losses yourself and recovery is tightly limited.","Small claims never reach you and your exposure is modest."],
 ["Warranty and indemnity insurance only",2,["{B} acknowledges that it has obtained the W&I Policy and agrees that its sole recourse in respect of any Claim shall be against the insurer under the W&I Policy.","{S}'s total liability for all Claims shall not exceed one pound (£1), save in the case of fraud.","{B} shall procure that the W&I Policy provides that the insurer waives its rights of subrogation against {S}, save in the case of fraud."],
  "You depend entirely on the insurer, and known issues and policy exclusions are not covered.","A clean exit. Your sale proceeds are safe.",{"W&I Policy":"the buyer-side warranty and indemnity insurance policy in the agreed form"}]]},

"ma-tax":{t:"Tax Covenant",g:["warranties"],
 d:"Who pays for tax liabilities of the company that relate to the period before completion.",
 n:"Tax claims usually carry a longer time limit than other claims, typically six or seven years, reflecting how long HMRC can reassess in cases of carelessness.",
 o:[
 ["Full covenant, outside the caps",-2,["{S} covenants to pay to {B} an amount equal to any liability of {T} to Tax arising in respect of, or by reference to, any income, profits or gains earned, accrued or received on or before Completion, or any event occurring on or before Completion, together with all reasonable costs incurred by {B} or {T} in connection with it.","The limitations in {R:ma-wlim} shall not apply to any claim under this clause, which may be brought at any time before the seventh (7th) anniversary of Completion."],
  "Tax relating to the period before you owned the company is the seller's problem, pound for pound.","Large exposure that lasts for seven years."],
 ["Covenant with standard exclusions",0,["{S} covenants to pay to {B} an amount equal to any liability of {T} to Tax arising in respect of, or by reference to, any income, profits or gains earned, accrued or received on or before Completion, or any event occurring on or before Completion.",["{S} shall not be liable under clause {N}.1 to the extent that:",["specific provision or reserve for the liability was made in the Accounts;","the liability arises in the ordinary course of business of {T} after the Accounts Date; or","the liability would not have arisen but for a voluntary act of {B} or {T} after Completion outside the ordinary course of business."]],"{S}'s total liability under this clause and for all Claims shall not exceed the Consideration, and no claim may be brought under this clause after the sixth (6th) anniversary of Completion."],
  "The market position. Strong protection with sensible exclusions.","The usual exclusions mean you do not pay twice for tax already accounted for."],
 ["Tax warranties only",2,["{B} acknowledges that its sole remedy in respect of Tax shall be a Claim for breach of the Warranties relating to Tax in {SC:war}, which shall be subject to the limitations in {R:ma-wlim}."],
  "You must prove a breach and a loss, and all the caps and thresholds apply.","Much lower exposure on tax."]]},

"ma-rc":{t:"Restrictive Covenants",g:["covenants"],
 d:"Stops the seller competing with, or poaching from, the business it has sold.",
 n:"Courts enforce restrictions given on a business sale more readily than in employment, but they must still go no further than reasonably necessary to protect the goodwill acquired.",
 o:[
 ["Three years, worldwide",-2,[["{S} undertakes to {B} that it shall not, and shall procure that no member of its group shall, directly or indirectly, for a period of three (3) years after Completion:",["anywhere in the world, carry on or be engaged, concerned or interested in any business which competes with the Business;","solicit or entice away from the Business any person who was a customer, client or supplier of the Business during the twelve (12) months before Completion; or","solicit or entice away any director or employee of the Business."]],"Each undertaking in this clause is a separate undertaking, and the parties agree that each is reasonable and necessary to protect the goodwill of the Business acquired by {B}."],
  "Strong protection for what you have paid for, though worldwide scope may be hard to justify.","Long and wide. It may stop you working in your field at all."],
 ["Two years, where the business trades",0,[["{S} undertakes to {B} that it shall not, and shall procure that no member of its group shall, directly or indirectly, for a period of two (2) years after Completion:",["in any country in which the Business was carried on during the twelve (12) months before Completion, carry on or be engaged in any business which competes with the Business;","solicit any person who was a customer of the Business during that period, with a view to providing goods or services which compete with the Business; or","solicit any employee of the Business earning more than £[●] a year."]],"Each undertaking in this clause is a separate undertaking, and the parties agree that each is reasonable and necessary to protect the goodwill of the Business acquired by {B}."],
  "The market position. Solid protection that a court is likely to uphold.","Proportionate restrictions that leave you free elsewhere."],
 ["Twelve months, non-solicitation only",2,["{S} undertakes to {B} that, for a period of twelve (12) months after Completion, it shall not solicit any senior employee of the Business to leave employment, save through general advertising not specifically targeted at such employees. No other restriction shall apply."],
  "The seller could set up a rival business the day after completion.","You are free to compete straight away."]]},

"ma-earn":{t:"Earn-out",g:["price-mechanisms"],
 d:"Makes part of the price depend on how the business performs after the sale, and controls how the buyer may run it in the meantime.",
 n:"English courts imply only limited duties into earn-outs, so any protection for the seller needs to be expressly drafted.",
 df:{"Earn-out Consideration":"the additional consideration, if any, calculated in accordance with {SC:earn}","Earn-out Period":"the period of [two (2)] financial years of {T} beginning immediately after Completion","EBITDA":"the earnings of {T} before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation for the relevant period, calculated in accordance with {SC:earn}"},
 o:[
 ["Buyer's absolute discretion",-2,["{B} shall pay to {S} the Earn-out Consideration, if any, calculated by reference to the EBITDA of {T} for the Earn-out Period.","{S} acknowledges that, following Completion, {B} shall be entitled to operate, integrate, restructure or dispose of the Business in its absolute discretion, and that {B} owes {S} no duty in respect of the amount of the Earn-out Consideration."],
  "Full freedom to integrate and restructure after completion.","The buyer's decisions could wipe out your earn-out with no comeback."],
 ["Good faith protections",0,["{B} shall pay to {S} the Earn-out Consideration, if any, calculated by reference to the EBITDA of {T} for the Earn-out Period.","{B} shall act in good faith in relation to the Earn-out and shall not take, or omit to take, any action with the primary purpose of reducing the Earn-out Consideration.","EBITDA shall be calculated using the accounting policies, principles and practices applied in the preparation of the Accounts."],
  "The market position. Limited constraints, and you can still run the business.","Protection against deliberate manipulation and accounting changes."],
 ["Operating covenants and acceleration",2,["{B} shall pay to {S} the Earn-out Consideration, if any, calculated by reference to the EBITDA of {T} for the Earn-out Period.",["Until the end of the Earn-out Period, {B} shall procure that {T}:",["carries on the Business as a separate business in the ordinary course and substantially in accordance with the Business Plan;","maintains separate accounting records for the Business; and","is provided with working capital sufficient to carry out the Business Plan."]],"The maximum Earn-out Consideration shall become immediately payable if {B} breaches this clause, or if {B} sells or transfers all or a material part of the Business, or {T} undergoes a change of control, before the end of the Earn-out Period."],
  "Your hands are tied for the whole earn-out period, and any breach triggers the full payment.","Strong protection for your deferred price.",{"Business Plan":"the business plan for {T} for the Earn-out Period in the agreed form"}]]},

/* ---------------- TSA ---------------- */
"tsa-scope":{t:"Provision of the Services",g:["carve-outs"],
 d:"How well the seller must provide the services that the sold business still depends on.",
 n:"The services schedule matters more than any clause. Gaps in it cause most TSA disputes, so list every service the business actually receives.",
 df:{"Good Industry Practice":GIP_DEF},
 o:[
 ["Pre-sale standard plus migration help",-2,[["{S} shall provide each Service to {B} during its Service Period:",["to at least the same scope, standard, quality, priority and level of service as it was provided to the Business during the twelve (12) months before Completion;","in accordance with Good Industry Practice; and","in compliance with all applicable laws."]],"{S} shall provide such assistance as {B} reasonably requires to migrate each Service to {B} or a replacement provider, without charge up to [●] person-days in aggregate."],
  "Service will not fall away after completion, and you get help moving off.","A high standard and an open-ended duty to help with migration."],
 ["Same as before completion",0,["{S} shall provide each Service to {B} during its Service Period in substantially the same manner, scope and standard as it was provided to the Business during the twelve (12) months before Completion.","{S} shall not be required to provide any Service to a higher standard than that at which it provides the equivalent service to its own retained business at the relevant time."],
  "The market position. Continuity of what you had before.","A clear benchmark you already meet."],
 ["Reasonable endeavours, as listed",2,["{S} shall use reasonable endeavours to provide the Services described in {SC:tsvc} during the applicable Service Period.",["{S} shall not be required to:",["provide any service not expressly described in {SC:tsvc};","make any change to its systems, processes, personnel or third-party arrangements; or","provide any Service in a manner that would breach any law or any agreement with a third party."]]],
  "A weak standard, and anything left out of the schedule is not provided.","Low risk and no obligation to improve anything."]]},

"tsa-term":{t:"Service Period",g:["carve-outs"],
 d:"How long the services last, whether they can be extended, and whether individual services can be stopped early.",
 o:[
 ["Long, with extensions",-2,["Each Service shall be provided from Completion for the initial Service Period specified for it in {SC:tsvc} or, if none is specified, for twenty-four (24) months.","{B} may extend the Service Period for any Service on up to two occasions, by up to six (6) months on each occasion, by giving {S} not less than sixty (60) days' written notice before the then current expiry date. The Charges shall not change during any extension.","{B} may terminate any individual Service by giving thirty (30) days' written notice, and the Charges shall be reduced accordingly."],
  "Plenty of runway, and flexibility to drop services as you migrate.","You may be supporting the business for three years."],
 ["Twelve months, one extension",0,["Each Service shall be provided from Completion for the initial Service Period specified for it in {SC:tsvc} or, if none is specified, for twelve (12) months.","{B} may extend the Service Period for any Service once, by up to six (6) months, by giving {S} not less than ninety (90) days' written notice. The Charges for any extension period shall be increased by ten per cent (10%).","{B} may terminate any individual Service by giving sixty (60) days' written notice, subject to reimbursing {S} for any stranded costs reasonably incurred."],
  "The market position. A reasonable runway with a safety net.","A defined end date, with a premium if migration overruns."],
 ["Six months fixed",2,["Each Service shall be provided from Completion for the fixed Service Period specified for it in {SC:tsvc}, which shall not exceed six (6) months and shall not be extended.","{B} may terminate the Services only as a whole and not in part, by giving ninety (90) days' written notice, and shall reimburse {S} for all stranded and wind-down costs."],
  "Very tight to separate the business, with no way to drop services early.","A quick, clean separation."]]},

"tsa-price":{t:"Charges",g:["carve-outs"],
 d:"How the transitional services are priced.",
 o:[
 ["At cost",-2,["The Charges for each Service shall be equal to the costs reasonably and properly incurred by {S} in providing it, calculated on the same basis as such costs were allocated to the Business before Completion, without any mark-up.","{S} shall provide reasonable supporting evidence of its costs on request."],
  "The cheapest option, priced the way the business was charged before the sale.","You subsidise the buyer's transition with your time and risk."],
 ["Cost plus a small margin",0,["The Charges for each Service shall be equal to the costs reasonably and properly incurred by {S} in providing it, plus a mark-up of five per cent (5%).","{S} shall provide reasonable supporting evidence of its costs on request."],
  "The market position. Fair, with a modest margin.","A modest return for providing services you do not normally sell."],
 ["Escalating margin",2,["The Charges for each Service shall be equal to the costs incurred by {S} in providing it plus ten per cent (10%), increasing to twenty-five per cent (25%) for any Service provided after the end of its initial Service Period.","{B} shall also reimburse {S} for all third-party costs incurred in providing the Services, including any licence fees."],
  "Expensive, and more so the longer migration takes.","A strong incentive for the buyer to migrate on time."]]},

"tsa-consent":{t:"Third Party Consents",g:["carve-outs"],
 d:"Who obtains, and pays for, the third-party consents needed to provide the services, such as software licence extensions.",
 n:"Software licences are often the hardest consents in a carve-out, because many restrict use to the licensee's own group.",
 df:{"Third Party Consent":"any consent, licence or approval required from a third party for {S} to provide a Service to {B}"},
 o:[
 ["{S} obtains and pays",-2,["{S} shall obtain, at its own cost, all Third Party Consents.","Until a Third Party Consent is obtained, {S} shall provide {B} with the benefit of the relevant Service by an alternative means of equivalent quality, at no additional charge."],
  "Consents are the seller's problem, and you still receive the service in the meantime.","You carry the cost and the risk of third parties holding out for payment."],
 ["Shared cost",0,["The parties shall use reasonable endeavours to obtain all Third Party Consents, and the costs of doing so shall be borne by {S} and {B} in equal shares.","If a Third Party Consent cannot be obtained, the parties shall co-operate in good faith to agree a reasonable alternative arrangement."],
  "The market position. Shared cost and a duty to find a workaround.","Shared cost, and no promise you cannot keep."],
 ["{B} pays, no obligation without consent",2,["{S} shall use reasonable endeavours to obtain the Third Party Consents, at {B}'s cost.","{S} shall have no obligation to provide any Service for which a Third Party Consent has not been obtained, and no liability for not providing it."],
  "You pay, and if a consent is refused you lose the service.","No cost and no liability for consents outside your control."]]},

/* ---------------- shareholders ---------------- */
"sha-res":{t:"Reserved Matters",g:["covenants"],
 d:"Decisions that the company cannot take without the investor's consent.",
 o:[
 ["Extensive veto rights",-2,[["{S} shall procure that the Company shall not, without {B}'s prior written consent:",["adopt or vary the annual budget or business plan;","allot or issue any shares or grant any right to subscribe for shares;","incur any borrowing in excess of £[●];","appoint or dismiss any employee whose annual remuneration exceeds £[●];","acquire or dispose of any business, company or material asset;","enter into any transaction with a shareholder or director, or any person connected with them; or","amend its Articles."]]],
  "Real control over how your investment is used.","Day-to-day decisions can be blocked by the investor."],
 ["Fundamental matters",0,[["{S} shall procure that the Company shall not, without {B}'s prior written consent:",["allot, issue, redeem or buy back any shares;","amend its Articles;","sell all or substantially all of its business or assets;","enter into any transaction with a shareholder or director, or any person connected with them, otherwise than on arm's length terms; or","be wound up, save where insolvent."]]],
  "The market position. Protection on decisions that change what you own.","You keep control of how the business is run."],
 ["Statutory minimum",2,["There shall be no reserved matters other than those decisions which require a special resolution of the Company's members under the Companies Act 2006."],
  "As a minority, you have almost no protection.","Full freedom to run the company."]]},

"sha-drag":{t:"Drag-along and Tag-along",g:["covenants"],
 d:"Whether a majority can force everyone to sell, and whether a minority can join any sale.",
 o:[
 ["Investor drag at any price",-2,["If the holders of a majority of the Investor Shares wish to transfer all their Investor Shares to a bona fide third-party purchaser, they may require all other shareholders to transfer all their Shares to that purchaser on the same terms."],
  "You control the exit and its timing.","You can be forced to sell at a price you think is too low."],
 ["Qualified majority drag, tag for all",0,["If the holders of seventy-five per cent (75%) of the Shares, including the holders of a majority of the Investor Shares, wish to transfer all their Shares to a bona fide third-party purchaser on arm's length terms, they may require all other shareholders to transfer their Shares to that purchaser on the same terms.","No transfer of Shares which would result in any person acquiring control of the Company may be made unless the purchaser offers to buy the Shares of all other shareholders on the same terms."],
  "The market position. A clear route to exit, and you can always join a sale.","A high threshold for a forced sale, and the right to join any change of control."],
 ["Founder consent required",2,["No shareholder may require any other shareholder to transfer its Shares without the prior written consent of {S}."],
  "You cannot force an exit if the founder refuses.","You can block any sale you do not support."]]},

"sha-pre":{t:"Anti-dilution",g:["covenants"],
 d:"Protects the investor if shares are later issued at a lower price than it paid.",
 n:"A broad-based weighted average is the usual position in UK venture investment documents.",
 o:[
 ["Full ratchet",-2,["If the Company issues any shares at a price per share below the price paid by {B} for the Investor Shares, {B} shall be issued such number of additional Investor Shares as would result in its Investor Shares having been subscribed at that lower price."],
  "Complete protection against a down round.","A down round could dilute you heavily."],
 ["Broad-based weighted average",0,["If the Company issues any shares at a price per share below the price paid by {B} for the Investor Shares, {B} shall be issued such number of additional Investor Shares as is calculated on a broad-based weighted average basis in accordance with the Articles."],
  "The market position. Fair protection that reflects how much new money came in.","Proportionate and widely accepted."],
 ["Pre-emption only",2,["{B} shall have a right of pre-emption on any new issue of shares in accordance with the Articles, but shall have no anti-dilution protection."],
  "You must invest more to avoid being diluted.","No extra dilution in a down round."]]},

/* ---------------- confidentiality agreements ---------------- */
"nda-def":{t:"Confidential Information",g:["confidentiality"],
 d:"Defines the information the recipient must protect.",
 o:[
 ["Marked information only",-2,[["In this Agreement, “Confidential Information” means information relating to {S} which is disclosed to {B} by or on behalf of {S} after the date of this Agreement in connection with the Purpose and which:",["if disclosed in writing or other tangible form, is clearly marked as confidential; or","if disclosed orally, is identified as confidential at the time of disclosure and confirmed as such in writing within fourteen (14) days."]]],
  "Clear limits on what you must protect.","Anything not marked in time is unprotected."],
 ["Marked or obviously confidential",0,["In this Agreement, “Confidential Information” means all information of a confidential nature relating to the business, affairs, customers, suppliers or plans of {S} or any member of its group which is disclosed to {B} or its Representatives by or on behalf of {S} in connection with the Purpose, whether before or after the date of this Agreement and in whatever form, and which is marked as confidential or would be regarded as confidential by a reasonable business person."],
  "The market position. A reasonable test that is easy to apply.","Covers everything that matters, even if unmarked."],
 ["Everything, including the discussions",2,[["In this Agreement, “Confidential Information” means all information of whatever nature and in whatever form relating to {S} or any member of its group which is disclosed to or obtained by {B} or its Representatives in connection with the Purpose, whether or not marked as confidential, together with:",["all analyses, compilations, notes, studies and other documents prepared by {B} or its Representatives which contain or reflect any such information; and","the fact that discussions are taking place in relation to the Proposed Transaction, and their status."]]],
  "Very wide. Hard to comply with fully and easy to breach.","Maximum protection."]]},

"nda-term":{t:"Duration",g:["confidentiality"],
 d:"How long the confidentiality obligations last.",
 o:[
 ["Two years from disclosure",-2,["The obligations in this Agreement shall continue in respect of each item of Confidential Information for two (2) years from the date of its disclosure."],
  "A short tail and a clear end date.","Your information is soon unprotected."],
 ["Three years from signing",0,["The obligations in this Agreement shall continue in force for three (3) years from the date of this Agreement."],
  "The market position.","A fair period of protection."],
 ["Without limit in time",2,["The obligations in this Agreement shall continue without limit in time, save that they shall cease to apply to any Confidential Information which falls within any of the exceptions in {R:*excl}."],
  "An obligation that never ends.","Permanent protection."]]},

"nda-return":{t:"Return and Destruction",g:["confidentiality"],
 d:"What happens to the information when the discussions end.",
 o:[
 ["On request, with practical retention",-2,["{B} shall, within thirty (30) days of a written request from {S}, return or destroy (at {B}'s option) all documents containing Confidential Information.",["{B} and its Representatives may retain Confidential Information:",["to the extent required by law, regulation or the rules of any professional body;","in board papers and minutes; and","in electronic back-up systems which are not readily accessible,"],"provided that any information so retained shall remain subject to this Agreement."]],
  "Practical and easy to comply with.","Copies of your information remain with the recipient."],
 ["Within ten Business Days, confirmed",0,["Within ten (10) Business Days of a written request from {S}, {B} shall return or destroy all documents containing Confidential Information and confirm in writing that it has done so, save that it may retain copies required by law or regulation or held in electronic back-up systems, which shall remain subject to this Agreement."],
  "The market position. Clear and workable.","Confirmation that your information has gone."],
 ["Everything, with director's certificate",2,[["{B} shall immediately on written request from {S}:",["return to {S} all documents and materials containing Confidential Information;","destroy all analyses, notes and other documents prepared by {B} or its Representatives which contain or reflect Confidential Information, and permanently erase all Confidential Information from its computer systems; and","deliver to {S} a certificate signed by a director of {B} confirming compliance with this clause."]],"Nothing in this clause permits {B} to retain any Confidential Information except to the extent required by law."],
  "Very difficult to comply with fully, particularly for IT back-ups.","Strong control over your information."]]},

"nda-nonsol":{t:"Non-solicitation",g:["covenants"],
 d:"Stops the recipient poaching the discloser's staff during and after the discussions.",
 n:"A non-solicitation covenant in a confidentiality agreement is enforceable only if it is reasonable in scope and duration.",
 o:[
 ["None",-2,["Nothing in this Agreement shall restrict {B} or any member of its group from soliciting, employing or engaging any person."],
  "You remain free to recruit as normal.","Your staff could be approached during the process."],
 ["Twelve months, people met",0,["{B} shall not, for a period of twelve (12) months from the date of this Agreement, directly or indirectly solicit or entice away from {S} any senior employee of {S} with whom it has had contact, or of whom it became aware, in connection with the Purpose.","This clause shall not prevent {B} from employing any person who responds to a general advertisement or recruitment campaign not specifically targeted at employees of {S}."],
  "The market position. A narrow, reasonable restriction.","Protects the people the bidder actually met."],
 ["Twenty-four months, all staff",2,["{B} shall not, for a period of twenty-four (24) months from the date of this Agreement, directly or indirectly solicit, employ or engage any employee of {S}, whether or not that employee responds to a general advertisement."],
  "A wide restriction that could block ordinary hiring.","Strong protection, though a court may find it too wide to enforce."]]},

/* ---------------- property ---------------- */
"ls-rent":{t:"Rent Review",g:["property"],
 d:"How and when the rent can change during the lease.",
 n:"Upward-only reviews remain common in England. They prevent the rent falling below the level payable before the review even if the market drops.",
 df:{"Review Date":"each fifth anniversary of the Term Commencement Date"},
 o:[
 ["Open market, upwards or downwards",-2,["The Rent shall be reviewed on each Review Date to the open market rent determined in accordance with {SC:omr}. With effect from each Review Date, the Rent shall be the open market rent so determined, whether higher or lower than the Rent payable immediately before that Review Date."],
  "You benefit if the market falls.","Your income could drop at review."],
 ["Upward-only open market",0,[["With effect from each Review Date, the Rent shall be the higher of:",["the Rent payable immediately before that Review Date; and","the open market rent on that Review Date, determined in accordance with {SC:omr}."]]],
  "The market position. The rent tracks the market, but only upwards.","Your income is protected against falls in the market."],
 ["CPI, with collar and cap",1,["On each anniversary of the Term Commencement Date, the Rent shall be increased by the percentage increase in CPI over the preceding twelve (12) months, provided that the increase in any year shall be not less than one per cent (1%) and not more than four per cent (4%)."],
  "Predictable increases every year, but they compound.","Steady growth with a guaranteed minimum.",{"CPI":"the Consumer Prices Index (all items) published by the Office for National Statistics, or any replacement index"}],
 ["RPI, upward-only, uncapped",2,["On each anniversary of the Term Commencement Date, the Rent shall be increased by the greater of two per cent (2%) and the percentage increase in RPI over the preceding twelve (12) months. The Rent shall not decrease."],
  "Your rent rises every year, potentially sharply. RPI usually runs ahead of CPI.","Guaranteed, inflation-linked growth.",{"RPI":"the Retail Prices Index (all items) published by the Office for National Statistics, or any replacement index"}]]},

"ls-break":{t:"Tenant's Break Option",g:["property"],
 d:"Lets the tenant end the lease early, and sets the conditions it must meet.",
 n:"Courts apply break conditions strictly, so even a small arrear or minor breach can defeat a break. A tenant has no implied right to a refund of rent paid for the period after the break date (Marks and Spencer v BNP Paribas [2015] UKSC 72).",
 o:[
 ["Two breaks, minimal conditions, refund",-2,["{B} may terminate this Lease on the third or fifth anniversary of the Term Commencement Date (each a “Break Date”) by giving {S} not less than six (6) months' written notice.","A break notice shall be effective provided only that, on the relevant Break Date, there are no arrears of the annual principal Rent.","Following termination under this clause, {S} shall refund to {B} any Rent and other sums paid in respect of any period after the Break Date."],
  "Flexible, very hard to defeat, and you get back rent paid for the period after you leave.","Your income could stop early."],
 ["One break, rent and vacant possession",0,["{B} may terminate this Lease on the fifth anniversary of the Term Commencement Date (the “Break Date”) by giving {S} not less than six (6) months' written notice.","A break notice shall be effective only if, on the Break Date, {B} has paid the annual principal Rent and gives vacant possession of the Premises."],
  "The market position. Workable, but you must leave the premises completely empty, and there is no refund of advance rent.","Reasonable protection when the tenant leaves."],
 ["Strict compliance",2,[["{B} may terminate this Lease on the fifth anniversary of the Term Commencement Date (the “Break Date”) by giving {S} not less than six (6) months' written notice, but only if on the Break Date:",["{B} has materially complied with all of the tenant covenants in this Lease;","{B} has paid all Rent and other sums due under this Lease; and","{B} gives vacant possession of the Premises, free of all occupiers and chattels."]],"Time shall be of the essence for the purposes of this clause."],
  "Easy to lose the break on a technicality.","Strong grounds to resist a break."]]},

"ls-repair":{t:"Repair",g:["property"],
 d:"How much repair work the tenant must do during, and at the end of, the lease.",
 n:"A covenant to “put” the premises into repair can require the tenant to improve them beyond their condition at the start. Damages for disrepair are capped at the reduction in value of the landlord's interest (Landlord and Tenant Act 1927, s.18(1)).",
 o:[
 ["Limited by schedule of condition",-2,["{B} shall keep the Premises in no worse state of repair and condition than that evidenced by the Schedule of Condition.","{B} shall not be liable to remedy any damage caused by an Insured Risk or any inherent defect."],
  "You only hand back what you took on.","You pay for any existing deterioration yourself.",{"Schedule of Condition":"the schedule of condition annexed to this Lease, prepared by [●] and dated [●]","Insured Risks":"fire, lightning, explosion, storm, flood, earthquake, aircraft, riot, malicious damage, terrorism and such other risks as {S} reasonably insures against from time to time"}],
 ["Good repair, sensible exclusions",0,["{B} shall keep the Premises in good and substantial repair and condition, save for damage caused by an Insured Risk (unless the insurance has been vitiated by any act or default of {B}) and any inherent defect."],
  "The market position. A standard obligation with fair exclusions.","A well-kept building and a familiar standard.",{"Insured Risks":"fire, lightning, explosion, storm, flood, earthquake, aircraft, riot, malicious damage, terrorism and such other risks as {S} reasonably insures against from time to time"}],
 ["Full repair, including structure",2,["{B} shall put and keep the Premises in good and substantial repair and condition and shall, where necessary, renew and rebuild them, including the structure and foundations and any inherent defect."],
  "You may have to improve the building beyond its condition when you took it.","The building is maintained entirely at the tenant's cost."]]},

"ls-alien":{t:"Assignment and Underletting",g:["property"],
 d:"Whether the tenant can transfer the lease, or sublet all or part of the premises.",
 n:"Where consent is not to be unreasonably withheld, the landlord must respond within a reasonable time and give reasons for any refusal (Landlord and Tenant Act 1988, s.1). Conditions for consent can be agreed in advance under s.19(1A) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1927.",
 o:[
 ["Flexible, group sharing allowed",-2,["{B} may assign or underlet the whole of the Premises, or underlet part of them, with {S}'s consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld or delayed.","{B} may share occupation of the Premises with any member of its group without {S}'s consent, provided that no relationship of landlord and tenant is created.","{S} shall not require an authorised guarantee agreement as a condition of consent to assignment unless the proposed assignee is of materially lower financial standing than {B}."],
  "Easy to restructure or leave.","Less control over who occupies your building."],
 ["Consent, guarantee where reasonable",0,["{B} shall not assign the whole of the Premises without {S}'s consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld or delayed.","For the purposes of section 19(1A) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1927, {S} may give consent to an assignment subject to a condition that {B} enters into an authorised guarantee agreement, where it is reasonable to require one."],
  "The market position. Workable, though you may have to guarantee whoever takes over.","Reasonable control and a backstop guarantee."],
 ["Strict conditions",2,["{B} shall not underlet or share occupation of part only of the Premises.",["{B} shall not assign the whole of the Premises without {S}'s consent. For the purposes of section 19(1A) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1927, it shall be a condition of any consent that:",["{B} enters into an authorised guarantee agreement;","the assignee provides a rent deposit equal to six (6) months' Rent; and","the assignee's net profits for each of its last three (3) financial years were at least three (3) times the annual Rent."]]],
  "Hard and expensive to get out of the lease.","Strong control and security."]]},

"ls-1954":{t:"Security of Tenure",g:["property"],
 d:"Whether the tenant has a statutory right to renew the lease when it ends.",
 n:"To exclude the right to renew, the landlord's warning notice and the tenant's declaration must be completed before the tenant is contractually bound (Landlord and Tenant Act 1954, s.38A). A clause in the lease alone is not enough.",
 o:[
 ["Protected tenancy",-2,["Nothing in this Lease shall exclude the provisions of sections 24 to 28 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1954 in relation to the tenancy created by this Lease."],
  "You have a statutory right to renew at the end of the term, which the landlord can only resist on limited grounds.","Regaining the premises at the end of the term may be slow, costly or impossible."],
 ["Contracted out",2,[["The parties confirm that:",["{S} served a notice on {B} in relation to the tenancy created by this Lease in the form, and within the time, required by section 38A(3)(a) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1954;","{B}, or a person duly authorised by it, made a declaration in the form required by section 38A(3)(b) of that Act; and","the provisions of sections 24 to 28 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1954 are excluded in relation to the tenancy created by this Lease."]]],
  "You must leave at the end of the term with no right to renew.","Full control over the premises when the lease ends."]]},

/* ---------------- employment ---------------- */
"emp-notice":{t:"Termination and Garden Leave",g:["covenants"],
 d:"How much notice each side must give, and the employer's rights to pay in lieu or require garden leave.",
 n:"An employer must give at least one week's notice for each complete year of service, up to twelve weeks (Employment Rights Act 1996, s.86).",
 df:{"Garden Leave":"any period during which {B} requires {S} not to attend work under this clause"},
 o:[
 ["Statutory minimum from employer",-2,["{B} may terminate the Employment by giving {S} not less than the minimum notice required by section 86 of the Employment Rights Act 1996. {S} may terminate the Employment by giving {B} not less than six (6) months' written notice.","{B} may, in its absolute discretion, terminate the Employment at any time with immediate effect by paying {S} a sum equal to the basic salary (excluding bonus, benefits and holiday accrual) that {S} would have received during the notice period or any unexpired part of it.","During all or any part of any notice period, {B} may require {S} to take Garden Leave, during which {S} shall remain an employee and bound by all duties of good faith and fidelity."],
  "Cheap and flexible to exit, while the executive stays bound for six months.","Little security, and a long period before you can move on."],
 ["Three months either way",0,["Either party may terminate the Employment by giving the other not less than three (3) months' written notice.","{B} may, in its absolute discretion, terminate the Employment with immediate effect by paying {S} a sum equal to the basic salary that {S} would have received during the notice period or any unexpired part of it.","During all or any part of any notice period, {B} may require {S} to take Garden Leave, during which {S} shall remain an employee and bound by all duties of good faith and fidelity."],
  "The market position for senior roles. Balanced, with flexibility to manage an exit.","Fair security and a reasonable route out."],
 ["Six months from employer, enhanced pay",2,["{B} may terminate the Employment by giving {S} not less than six (6) months' written notice. {S} may terminate the Employment by giving {B} not less than one (1) month's written notice.","If {B} terminates the Employment without giving full notice, it shall pay {S}, within fourteen (14) days of the Termination Date, a sum equal to the salary, bonus and cost to {B} of providing all contractual benefits for the notice period or its unexpired part.","{B} may not require {S} to take Garden Leave without {S}'s consent."],
  "Costly to exit, and the executive can leave on a month's notice.","Strong security, and a guaranteed payment if you are let go early."]]},

"emp-rc":{t:"Post-Termination Restrictions",g:["covenants"],
 d:"Limits on what the employee may do after leaving.",
 n:"Restrictions are void unless they go no further than reasonably necessary to protect a legitimate business interest. A court will not rewrite an over-wide clause, but may remove words that can be cut out without changing its meaning (Tillman v Egon Zehnder [2019] UKSC 32).",
 df:{"Restricted Business":"those parts of the business of {B} and any Group Company with which {S} was materially involved during the Relevant Period","Restricted Client":"any person who was a client of {B} or any Group Company during the Relevant Period and with whom {S} had material dealings","Relevant Period":"the period of twelve (12) months immediately before the Termination Date"},
 o:[
 ["Twelve months, full suite",-2,[["{S} shall not, for a period of twelve (12) months after the Termination Date, directly or indirectly:",["be employed or engaged in, or provide services to, any Restricted Business in competition with {B} within the United Kingdom;","solicit, or deal with, any Restricted Client in competition with {B}; or","solicit or entice away from {B} any employee earning more than £[●] a year with whom {S} worked during the Relevant Period."]],"Each restriction in this clause is a separate obligation and is severable from the others."],
  "Strong protection, though a twelve-month non-compete is at risk of being struck out.","Could keep you out of your industry for a year."],
 ["Six months, reduced by garden leave",0,[["{S} shall not, directly or indirectly:",["for six (6) months after the Termination Date, be employed or engaged in any Restricted Business in a role similar to that held by {S} during the Relevant Period;","for twelve (12) months after the Termination Date, solicit any Restricted Client in competition with {B}; or","for twelve (12) months after the Termination Date, solicit or entice away from {B} any employee earning more than £[●] a year with whom {S} worked during the Relevant Period."]],"Each period in this clause shall be reduced by any period of Garden Leave.","Each restriction in this clause is a separate obligation and is severable from the others."],
  "The market position. Realistic, and much more likely to be enforced.","Proportionate, and limited to people and clients you actually dealt with."],
 ["Light non-solicitation",2,["{S} shall not, for a period of six (6) months after the Termination Date, solicit any Restricted Client in competition with {B}. No other restriction shall apply after the Termination Date."],
  "The employee can join a competitor immediately.","Free to work wherever you choose."]]},

/* ---------------- finance ---------------- */
"fin-cov":{t:"Financial Covenants",g:["finance"],
 d:"The financial ratios the borrower must keep to, and whether a breach can be cured.",
 df:{"Relevant Period":"each period of twelve (12) months ending on a Quarter Date","Quarter Date":"each of 31 March, 30 June, 30 September and 31 December","Leverage":"the ratio of Total Net Debt on the last day of a Relevant Period to EBITDA for that Relevant Period","Total Net Debt":"the aggregate financial indebtedness of the Group less its cash","EBITDA":"the consolidated operating profit of the Group before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation"},
 o:[
 ["Incurrence test only",-2,["No maintenance financial covenant shall apply.","{B} shall not incur any additional financial indebtedness or make any dividend or distribution unless, on a pro forma basis taking that indebtedness or distribution into account, Leverage would not exceed [●]:1."],
  "No risk of default from a single weak quarter.","Little early warning if the business weakens."],
 ["Leverage covenant with equity cure",0,["{B} shall ensure that Leverage in respect of each Relevant Period does not exceed 4.00:1.","Leverage shall be tested on each Quarter Date by reference to the compliance certificate delivered with the quarterly financial statements.","If Leverage exceeds the level in clause {N}.1, {B} may, within twenty (20) Business Days of the due date of the relevant compliance certificate, procure that new equity is contributed and treated as reducing Total Net Debt, provided that this right is not exercised in consecutive Relevant Periods or more than twice during the life of the Facility."],
  "The market position. Room to absorb a bad patch and a way to fix a breach.","A meaningful early warning, with a capped cure right."],
 ["Tight covenants, no cure",2,[["{B} shall ensure that, in respect of each Relevant Period:",["Leverage does not exceed 3.00:1; and","Interest Cover is not less than 4.00:1."]],"No equity cure or other right to remedy a breach of this clause shall apply."],
  "A small dip in trading could put you in default.","Early control if the business starts to struggle.",{"Interest Cover":"the ratio of EBITDA to net finance charges for a Relevant Period"}]]},

"fin-eod":{t:"Events of Default",g:["finance"],
 d:"The events that allow the lender to cancel the facility and demand immediate repayment.",
 n:"Drafting follows Loan Market Association conventions, which most UK lenders use as their starting point.",
 o:[
 ["Narrow, with thresholds",-2,[["Each of the following is an Event of Default:",["{B} fails to pay any amount due under a Finance Document within five (5) Business Days of its due date;","{B} fails to comply with {R:fin-cov}, and the failure is not cured in accordance with that clause;","{B} fails to comply with any other material obligation under a Finance Document and does not remedy the failure within twenty (20) Business Days of {S} giving notice of it;","any financial indebtedness of {B} exceeding £[5,000,000] in aggregate is declared due before its maturity by reason of an event of default; or","{B} is unable to pay its debts as they fall due, or any insolvency proceedings are commenced against it, other than proceedings which are frivolous or vexatious and are discharged within twenty-one (21) days."]],"At any time after an Event of Default has occurred and while it is continuing, {S} may cancel the Facility and declare the Loan immediately due and payable."],
  "Fewer triggers, and time to fix problems before the lender can act.","Less ability to act early."],
 ["Loan Market Association standard",0,[["Each of the following is an Event of Default:",["{B} fails to pay any amount due under a Finance Document on its due date, unless the failure is caused by an administrative or technical error and payment is made within three (3) Business Days;","{B} fails to comply with {R:fin-cov};","{B} fails to comply with any other obligation under a Finance Document and does not remedy the failure within fifteen (15) Business Days;","any representation made by {B} in a Finance Document is incorrect or misleading in any material respect when made;","any financial indebtedness of {B} exceeding £[1,000,000] in aggregate is not paid when due or is declared due before its maturity by reason of an event of default; or","{B} is or is deemed unable to pay its debts, or any insolvency proceedings are commenced against it."]],"At any time after an Event of Default has occurred and while it is continuing, {S} may cancel the Facility and declare the Loan immediately due and payable."],
  "The market position.","The market position, with the standard grace periods."],
 ["Wide, including material adverse change",2,[["Each of the following is an Event of Default:",["{B} fails to pay any amount due under a Finance Document on its due date;","{B} fails to comply with any obligation under a Finance Document;","any financial indebtedness of {B} is not paid when due, or is capable of being declared due before its maturity;","{B} is or is deemed unable to pay its debts, or any insolvency proceedings are commenced against it; or","any event or circumstance occurs which {S} reasonably believes has or is reasonably likely to have a material adverse effect on the business or financial condition of {B} or its ability to perform its obligations."]],"At any time after an Event of Default, {S} may cancel the Facility and declare the Loan immediately due and payable."],
  "The lender can call a default on its own judgment, and there are no grace periods.","Maximum control and the ability to act early."]]},

"fin-prepay":{t:"Voluntary Prepayment",g:["finance"],
 d:"Whether the borrower can repay early, and what it costs.",
 o:[
 ["Any time, without premium",-2,["{B} may, by giving {S} not less than five (5) Business Days' prior notice, prepay the whole or any part of the Loan (but, if in part, by a minimum amount of £[●]) without premium or penalty.","Any prepayment shall be made together with accrued interest on the amount prepaid."],
  "You can refinance freely when rates fall.","Your expected interest income can disappear at short notice."],
 ["Soft call for six months",0,["{B} may, by giving {S} not less than five (5) Business Days' prior notice, prepay the whole or any part of the Loan.","Any prepayment made within six (6) months of the date of utilisation shall be made together with a premium of one per cent (1%) of the amount prepaid, and all prepayments shall be made together with accrued interest on the amount prepaid."],
  "The market position. A small cost to refinance early.","Short-term protection of your return."],
 ["Make-whole, then step-down",2,["{B} may prepay the whole or any part of the Loan by giving {S} not less than ten (10) Business Days' prior notice.","Any prepayment made within twenty-four (24) months of the date of utilisation shall be made together with the Make-Whole Amount. Any prepayment made in the third or fourth year after utilisation shall be made together with a premium of two per cent (2%) or one per cent (1%) respectively of the amount prepaid."],
  "Very expensive to refinance for the first four years.","Your full return is protected.",{"Make-Whole Amount":"the present value of all interest that would have accrued on the amount prepaid from the date of prepayment to the second anniversary of the date of utilisation, discounted at the gilt rate plus 0.50 per cent. per annum"}]]}
};
